{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted","id":1201880,"title":"Is the Technocracy Short Sighted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-01T02:50:01-07:00","id":1201880,"title":"Is the Technocracy Short Sighted?","content":"<br /> <br /> Can't travel faster than light.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even reaching semi-light speed seems impossible.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cryogenic stasis for living beings also seems like a work of science fiction.<br /> <br /> <br /> Scientific 'teleportation' would actually kill you and produce a clone to replace you every time you use it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Going through a wormhole would most likely kill you as your atoms spaghettify.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even though we've discovered other planets capable of sustaining life, it would take eons (from our perspective) for us to reach them.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's no vessel in human history that has the storage space necessary to sustain a voyage taking 10's of thousands of years.<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically, we have no practical means of venturing beyond our star system and colonizing other worlds once we've expended the resources on Earth. That means we're stuck here waiting for the sun to burn out and incinerate us in the blast of the super nova.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thinking about all of this, I can't help but feel like the Technocracy and their progenitors may have signed us all up for a Faustian deal.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a short term solution, their version of consensus allowed humanity to become the dominant power of this world. But the long term consequences may have doomed us as a species, along with everything else living on this planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-01-2018, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T03:15:33-07:00","id":1201884,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if they ever use your exact example, but yeah, it's kinda the point of Revised that the Technocrats have constricted their own long-term ability to introduce new technology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T03:20:53-07:00","id":1201885,"title":"","content":"This assumes that the limitations of sleeper science are choices the Technocracy has made and not some combination of Paradox backlash and the current limitations of Consensus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T04:38:08-07:00","id":1201891,"title":"","content":"I don't see this as short-sightedness. I see this as a difference in priorities.<br /> <br /> Sure, they've made it so humans can't feasibly travel vast interstellar distances to other worlds. But, by that same token, they've also made it so ALIENS can't either. The Consensus has been stacked towards there being other worlds, but against the likelihood of those beings being able to show up. A state of affairs that dictates the rules of engagement that outsiders can play by.<br /> <br /> Why do you think the Gauntlet is so thick these days? Why do you think &quot;aliens&quot; only show up in rural or wilderness areas, where few witnesses are around or would be believed?<br /> <br /> Remember, given how it was basically impossible for most people to leave Earth until a few centuries ago (other than Mages, of course, who don't count), it was sort of up in the air how distant the stars were. It's why people often called planets like Mars and Jupiter &quot;stars&quot;, as those points of light weren't terribly bigger or smaller than the &quot;fixed stars&quot;. For all the Consensus knew, you'd reach another world by traveling a small distance from Earth, indeed.<br /> <br /> What the Technocracy did was sell people on the idea that no, you can't just pop over to Alpha Centari on a whim. That, beyond the planets in our solar system, there were not inhabitable worlds anywhere near Earth. Once that's established, most people were convinced, in any serious discussion, that space travel to other worlds is simply not feasible.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union's first priority is the safety of the human race, and its protection against both the threats from outside, and from within. That even includes, yes, protecting mankind from itself. Making it that hard to reach other worlds doesn't just make it harder for &quot;aliens&quot; to show up on Earth. It also makes it so overzealous humans don't rocket themselves into space before they are ready, and cause troubles among the stars (trouble that could easily then follow back to Earth). You think if light speed were easier to overcome or the distance were smaller, that the US and USSR wouldn't be racing into Deep Space right now? You think Elon Musk wouldn't be using Space X to colonize other galaxies?<br /> <br /> Sure, there are opportunities in space, but also dangers. Awful dangers. Horrors birthed from the farthest stars and darkest depths, waiting for mankind to stumble on them. And if people knew they could get to other worlds, they'd be expecting alien races. Ergo, they would find what they expected to find. Cue the galactic empires looking to annex Earth, bug aliens looking to devour Earth like locusts, or eldritch horrors looking to teach Earthlings new ways to kill and sin, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far at the Union is concerned, any thoughts of colonization beyond our solar system will have to wait until mankind has built up its conquering ability. And remember, at least a few of the limitations mentioned in the first post are engineering problems. Once the Union thinks humanity is ready, scientists will &quot;just happen&quot; to crack things like breaking lightspeed or cryogenics. &quot;Technology Holds All The Answers&quot; is a popular Paradigm for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T05:31:19-07:00","id":1201895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1201891#post1201891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As far at the Union is concerned, any thoughts of colonization beyond our solar system will have to wait until mankind has built up its conquering ability. And remember, at least a few of the limitations mentioned in the first post are engineering problems. Once the Union thinks humanity is ready, scientists will &quot;just happen&quot; to crack things like breaking lightspeed or cryogenics. &quot;Technology Holds All The Answers&quot; is a popular Paradigm for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Union had Faster than Light travel and space colonies beyond the solar system before the the Reckoning, and has access to all sorts of things Sleeper science currently finds impossible. The current situation I would among Sleeper scientists is not the intended long term goal. I'm sure the Time table includes things like &quot;Discover hyper space by 2053..&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T07:55:49-07:00","id":1201916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1201891#post1201891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see this as short-sightedness. I see this as a difference in priorities.<br /> <br /> Sure, they've made it so humans can't feasibly travel vast interstellar distances to other worlds. But, by that same token, they've also made it so ALIENS can't either. The Consensus has been stacked towards there being other worlds, but against the likelihood of those beings being able to show up. A state of affairs that dictates the rules of engagement that outsiders can play by.<br /> <br /> Why do you think the Gauntlet is so thick these days? Why do you think &quot;aliens&quot; only show up in rural or wilderness areas, where few witnesses are around or would be believed?<br /> <br /> Remember, given how it was basically impossible for most people to leave Earth until a few centuries ago (other than Mages, of course, who don't count), it was sort of up in the air how distant the stars were. It's why people often called planets like Mars and Jupiter &quot;stars&quot;, as those points of light weren't terribly bigger or smaller than the &quot;fixed stars&quot;. For all the Consensus knew, you'd reach another world by traveling a small distance from Earth, indeed.<br /> <br /> What the Technocracy did was sell people on the idea that no, you can't just pop over to Alpha Centari on a whim. That, beyond the planets in our solar system, there were not inhabitable worlds anywhere near Earth. Once that's established, most people were convinced, in any serious discussion, that space travel to other worlds is simply not feasible.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union's first priority is the safety of the human race, and its protection against both the threats from outside, and from within. That even includes, yes, protecting mankind from itself. Making it that hard to reach other worlds doesn't just make it harder for &quot;aliens&quot; to show up on Earth. It also makes it so overzealous humans don't rocket themselves into space before they are ready, and cause troubles among the stars (trouble that could easily then follow back to Earth). You think if light speed were easier to overcome or the distance were smaller, that the US and USSR wouldn't be racing into Deep Space right now? You think Elon Musk wouldn't be using Space X to colonize other galaxies?<br /> <br /> Sure, there are opportunities in space, but also dangers. Awful dangers. Horrors birthed from the farthest stars and darkest depths, waiting for mankind to stumble on them. And if people knew they could get to other worlds, they'd be expecting alien races. Ergo, they would find what they expected to find. Cue the galactic empires looking to annex Earth, bug aliens looking to devour Earth like locusts, or eldritch horrors looking to teach Earthlings new ways to kill and sin, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far at the Union is concerned, any thoughts of colonization beyond our solar system will have to wait until mankind has built up its conquering ability. And remember, at least a few of the limitations mentioned in the first post are engineering problems. Once the Union thinks humanity is ready, scientists will &quot;just happen&quot; to crack things like breaking lightspeed or cryogenics. &quot;Technology Holds All The Answers&quot; is a popular Paradigm for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If I thought the Technocracy had any redeeming features before, those are pretty much gone now.<br /> <br /> So not only did they screw over humanity's potential in the name of 'protecting' us, but they also saw fit to screw over the potential of countless other sentient life forms.<br /> <br /> And they jumped to the conclusion that these life forms were out to kill us, rather than being interested in establishing intergalactic diplomacy?<br /> <br /> If they don't get to conquer the galaxy, then nobody does. That's their line of thinking?<br /> <br /> These guys are massive dicks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T10:02:56-07:00","id":1201952,"title":"","content":"Well, it is Mage, so you are entitled to your opinion. However, I tend to take a view of the Technocracy as a group that seeks to protect humans. There;s a good debate in Native American history about whether there was a 'middle ground' between Europeans and Native Americans. In one book in the debate, <i>Into the American Woods</i>, James Merrill talks about how the spaces in between the forests were known to both Native Americans and early European settlers to be filled with dangerous things. So, while there is no such thing as a 'middle ground,' there was a shared view that the American woods were a place you had to go through to reach other areas. To make peace, you had to go through the woods.<br /> <br /> Both the Traditions and the Technocracy see dangerous things out there and want a Gauntlet. The Traditions want a thinner Gauntlet, because they do believe in spirits. Not all of those spirits are bad, but most humans could not survive the material and spirit worlds overlapping completely. The Technocracy wants control, so they pretty much kill anything spiritual or reframe it so they can explain it as technology.<br /> <br /> Given the life discussed in Mage as being in the Umbra, I'd be wanting to make it hard to get there as well. Though the mages could be projecting fears out into the unknown, and thus be poor at getting society where it is going. So much of what is dangerous is perception. . .<br /> <br /> Oh, and I have Elon Musk as a Technocrat with his Mars promotion. Those currently exploding Tesla cars, well that's just the Sons of Ether attacking his assets. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T12:40:16-07:00","id":1201990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1201916#post1201916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These guys are massive dicks!</div> </div> </div> </div>They're the major antagonists of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T13:20:09-07:00","id":1201999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1201916#post1201916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> If I thought the Technocracy had any redeeming features before, those are pretty much gone now.<br /> <br /> So not only did they screw over humanity's potential in the name of 'protecting' us, but they also saw fit to screw over the potential of countless other sentient life forms.<br /> <br /> And they jumped to the conclusion that these life forms were out to kill us, rather than being interested in establishing intergalactic diplomacy?<br /> <br /> If they don't get to conquer the galaxy, then nobody does. That's their line of thinking?<br /> <br /> These guys are massive dicks!</div> </div> </div> </div>They were/are Jetting around in FTL machines, much of what of what you hold out as being impossible are just current failures on the part of Sleepers to accept the true Paradigm of the Techncracy. Eventually they will include FTL, Teleporation, stasis.. and it will all work. They promise.<br /> <br /> Also resleeving, Forking. You'll be immortal in the body of your choice. And its going to be real immortality, not that &quot;your soul goes some place&quot; bullshit. They will have back ups of you. Its all coming. Really. They will be able to fix your mind of all dangerous and unhealthy instincts that have only caused you pain. The Technocracy cares.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for intergalactic Diplomacy. So Far they've Found &quot;Lovecraft was Right&quot; about the cosmos based on their discoveries with the occasional dose of &quot;This energy being is claiming to be Zeus again and wants to impregnate half our Crew&quot; and beings that spread the worst of the human condition attempting to mutate human forms to become something more horrific to continue to spread misery beyond the safety of the Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T13:22:01-07:00","id":1202000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1201952#post1201952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and I have Elon Musk as a Technocrat with his Mars promotion. Those currently exploding Tesla cars, well that's just the Sons of Ether attacking his assets. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Paradox because they haven't quite worked everything out..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T13:37:20-07:00","id":1202004,"title":"","content":"I think that the consensus (no pun intended) among the player base seems to be that, pre-20th century, both the Union and the Traditions were equally bad choices for humanity. Then the SoE and the VA jumped ship, meaning that the Union lost two of its big redeeming qualities and the Traditions went from being luddites to arguably more tech-friendly than the Technocracy. So most of the arguments that can be made are basically &quot;it's not that the Union is <i>evil</i>, per se, but a Tradition victory would probably still be a better outcome&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the end, losing the two future technomancer Traditions basically removed any hope of the Technocracy pushing the Consensus to the point they'd like and they still have yet to realize why.<br /> <br /> And this is coming from a self-professed Technocratic sympathizer!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 04-01-2018, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T13:54:02-07:00","id":1202010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202004#post1202004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the consensus (no pun intended) among the player base seems to be that, pre-20th century, both the Union and the Traditions were equally bad choices for humanity. Then the SoE and the VA jumped ship, meaning that the Union lost two of its big redeeming qualities and the Traditions went from being luddites to arguably more tech-friendly than the Technocracy. So most of the arguments that can be made are basically &quot;it's not that the Union is <i>evil</i>, per se, but a Tradition victory would probably still be a better outcome&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the end, losing the two future technomancer Traditions basically removed any hope of the Technocracy pushing the Consensus to the point they'd like and they still have yet to realize why.<br /> <br /> And this is coming from a self-professed Technocratic sympathizer!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's the consensus at all. You're saying the Order of Reason during the HEIGHTS of Colonialism was a better choice than &quot;please don't murder our people or introduce new diseases&quot; or that groups like the Order of Hermes were as intrinsically Ludditic as some people try to push. Plus there probably were OOR members who were sympathetic to the Luddite cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T14:10:41-07:00","id":1202016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1201990#post1201990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're the major antagonists of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes, and from what I can tell, they're leading us on the path towards Warhammer 40k.<br /> <br /> Bare in mind that magic in the 40k universe operates in similar fashion to how it works in Mage. It's powered by the belief of whoever's casting it, giving them the ability to warp reality as they desire. Daemons (yes, that's the proper spelling) and the dark gods are also literal figments of imagination formed out of the collective consciousness of all sentient races.<br /> <br /> So this Emperor (who's so powerful, he's basically a god) thought that keeping humanity ignorant of the supernatural was the best way to steer them towards greatness, but it only succeeded in making things easier for the supernatural to manipulate humanity towards their own purposes. People started falling victim to Daemonic influence, because they had no idea that Daemons existed, much less what they were trying to do. They came to them in the guise of friendship, offering them answers to questions the Emperor insisted on being cryptic about.<br /> <br /> Next thing you know, half the empire is in open rebellion, the Emperor is mortally wounded and over the course of the next 10,000 years, the Empire of Mankind degenerates into backwards extremists who literally pray to technology in order to make it function properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-01-2018, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T14:21:24-07:00","id":1202017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202016#post1202016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and from what I can tell, they're leading us on the path towards Warhammer 40k.</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T14:27:11-07:00","id":1202019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202016#post1202016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, and from what I can tell, they're leading us on the path towards Warhammer 40k.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Star Trek.. well not star Trek thanks Syndicate for ruining that..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T14:40:34-07:00","id":1202025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1201916#post1201916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So not only did they screw over humanity's potential in the name of 'protecting' us, but they also saw fit to screw over the potential of countless other sentient life forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy are humanists, first and foremost. Protecting humanity comes before anything else, just as the Union expects every other potential sapient beings to be protecting itself before anything else. Given that the Union tends to be cynical, assuming that other beings are preoccupied with their own self-interest comes naturally to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And they jumped to the conclusion that these life forms were out to kill us, rather than being interested in establishing intergalactic diplomacy? </div> </div> </div>It's not really &quot;jumping to the conclusion&quot; if the Technocracy, in one form or another, has been making forays into the Umbra for centuries, and they've generally encountered &quot;Lovecraft was right&quot; as a rule. They aren't being paranoid or xenophobic when their fears tend to pan out.<br /> <br /> Maybe their own practices predispose Umbral creatures to despise them. Maybe some werewolves have been making sure that the Void Engineers only ever encounter dangerous stuff in the Umbra, and not the idyllic gardens or peaceful races. Maybe the Technocracy's own fears shape what they find, as the nature of the place tends to make an Umbral traveler find what they expect to. Or maybe the Void Engineers have been very unlucky.<br /> <br /> Regardless, no matter if their experiences are skewed towards the negative, those are still their experiences, and they've made an entirely valid reaction to being confronted with a galaxy that largely hates them and wants them to die. Even though I'm sure the Void Engineers encounter plenty of peaceful or benign creatures too, on the whole they see the Void as a dangerous and unwelcoming place in aggregate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they don't get to conquer the galaxy, then nobody does. That's their line of thinking? </div> </div> </div>I must remind you, there IS no normal space beyond a certain distance from the Earth. It's ALL Umbra beyond Mars.<br /> <br /> Sure, within the context of that space, there are vast distances to the next galaxy. In terms of what we call the non-Umbra Material World, though, humanity is taking up a relatively small chunk of cosmic real estate. And the Union knows this. It's the arrangement they prefer. When taken from this line of thinking, the Void beyond the world is mostly in another dimension. It's only the Sleepers who are under the impression that space is an uninterrupted expanse you can just go to, if you pilot a shuttle far enough.<br /> <br /> As such, the Union knows that &quot;preventing alien races from exploring the galaxy&quot; doesn't really work that way. It requires a certain degree of Enlightenment to break into the Horizon, and yet more to reach the Deep Umbra. And recall, in the Deep Umbra, <i>Here Be Cthulhu</i>. Nephandi ride living abominations as their space craft, and any kind of rules of Reality as people understand it break down. To the Union, the farther you travel, the more incomprehensibly alien you get, and not in a good way.<br /> <br /> Moreover, even if we assume that beyond the Deep Umbra, there are other sapient beings, they would probably be inhabiting their own Tellurian, with its own set of beliefs. From the Technocracy's perspective, those guys can attend to their own affairs, because THEIR beliefs make the rules for THEIR part of the cosmos. Creating a Paradigm of vast interstellar distance only really matters when it comes to strengthening Earth's Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T20:38:27-07:00","id":1202118,"title":"","content":"Even given the metaphysics of Mage, ignorance is rarely a productive way to protect people. It usually cripples people's ability to deal with circumstances and events they should have been aware of and trained for. But the infantilization of the human race is a key element of the Technocrat philosophy so it makes sense that they'd do it despite the consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T21:55:35-07:00","id":1202129,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to leave this <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIMV6E8OxG8&amp;list=PLIIOUpOge0Lvr26RCeM_6mq72KFhPWEkG\" target=\"_blank\">here...</a><br /> <br /> Basically it answers all these issues on this site. Its amazing I've been binging it for a week. So its really more of a bit past a hundred years to colonize nearby stars, with thousands for more distant stars, and even colonizing into Andromeda is feasible in the future, just develop the Laser Highway system. So pretty much first we need fusion, then mine the asteroids, and then we can blast off to Andromeda and Tau Seti. And even a Dyson swarm is feasible by modern principles, in theory allowing space and reasources for literally trillions of habitats that can each hold millions of people, and by the time we do that boom nutzo levels of sci fi.<br /> <br /> Oh and the principles of we have also means its actually conceivable to mine the sun through Starlifting, and even Move the Sun through high powered lasers, so pretty much brute force the solutions.<br /> <br /> And that is just the sleeper science, The Techies will have access to impossibilities of Enlightened science and will have essentially stabilized worlds and populations under their control beyond conventional reach providing resources to secret police/NWO the future of the Star Trekky humanity... as long as they pogrom all dem reality deviants.<br /> <br /> Now things can get sticky if sleepers make contact with Aliens or discover FTL...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T05:22:50-07:00","id":1202198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202118#post1202118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even given the metaphysics of Mage, ignorance is rarely a productive way to protect people. It usually cripples people's ability to deal with circumstances and events they should have been aware of and trained for. But the infantilization of the human race is a key element of the Technocrat philosophy so it makes sense that they'd do it despite the consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hence, my Warhammer 40k analogy, since that is literally exactly what happened to the Empire of Mankind in that universe. Humanity was well on its way to conquering the galaxy. They had an empire that spanned across literally billions of planets. The various alien races were being pushed back or destroyed, belief in the supernatural was almost completely abandoned in favor of secular reasoning and hard sciences. Pretty much everything the Technocracy is currently striving to accomplish.<br /> <br /> Then the Emperor's greatest followers learned that there were a few trust issues between them, which lead to them questioning their faith in him. Admittedly, the Emperor's grand plan was to create a pyschic barrier that would have basically neutered the Chaos Gods' influence, but he refused to divulge that information to even his most trusted warriors, whom he genetically modified using his own DNA and who revered him like he was their own father. These seeds of doubt were all the Chaos Gods needed to manipulate half the empire (which again, billions of inhabited planets) to turn against him, thus resulting in a civil war that even 10,000 years later, they have not recovered from.<br /> <br /> In fact, it's so bad that humanity began to see technology itself as being inherently magical and started praying to it on a regular basis. If your gun jams when you pull the trigger, it's not due to a technical malfunction, it's because the spirit of the gun isn't angry enough to spit a chunk of exploding metal at your designated target. So you have to perform a war chant in order to psyche the spirit up for battle. And, because the supernatural in 40k is fueled by the thoughts and emotions of those who believe in it, this actually gets the gun working again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-02-2018, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T07:48:33-07:00","id":1202220,"title":"","content":"Going on about something that's going to happen in -- worst estimate -- four billion years*...is this an April Fool's post?<br /> <br /> Because, I'ma take this seriously for a minute. The Technocracy already has extrasolar colonies, populated by enough EC's to create a localized Consensus and be self-sustaining. Sparing that, if humanity survives that long, by the time the Sun starts expanding Jupiter's moons will be well within its habitable zone and would probably make nice places to live with a little terraforming and/or habitat construction.<br /> <br /> <i>[* Yes, I know most astronomers' and physicists' estimates are that the Earth will be destroyed by the Sun going nova between five to seven billion years from now. But, that doesn't take into account the possibility of the Earth's orbit being shifted well before then due to the effects of increased solar winds and the Sun's loss of mass during its expansionary period. Nor the fact that, long before this happens, the Sun's habitable zone will be pushed outwards to Jupiter's orbit.]</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202198#post1202198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...And, because the supernatural in 40k is fueled by the thoughts and emotions of those who believe in it, this actually gets the gun working again!</div> </div> </div> </div>That works for Eldar and Orks, who are all innately psykers on some level, not humans. Not even human Force weapons work that way. What happened, is that all but a small cross-section of humanity (the Adeptus Mechanicus) forgot how AI works, or even that AI exists. The Adeptus Mechanicus knows full well what's up; it just happens to be the case such knowledge is heretical enough to get even <i>Mars</i> on the Exterminatus short list.<br /> <br /> Thus, the Adeptus Mechanicus promulgates a big lie (even internally, invoking heavy doublethink and newspeak among their number) there is no such thing as AI, but instead machines have spirits of their own that have to be prayed to and appeased to work. Less knowledgeable people take that big lie and run with it, attributing any mechanical fault or software glitch to the machine spirits. Or, for that matter, how vehicles up to and including titans &quot;become full of the Emperor's righteous fury and will themselves to fight on, even when the crew is completely incapacitated or dead&quot;. The AM lies their asses off about how STC's work, and how hardware produced by STC's work, or that anything bigger than a Mars-pattern boltgun has onboard AI for standard operation and troubleshooting procedure.<br /> <br /> <i>[Edit, for those unfamiliar with Warhammer 40K. STC stands for Standard Template Construct, which was in-universe humanity's key to conquering the stars. STC's were, in their purest form, miniaturized refineries and manufactories coupled with an AI-assisted database containing standardized blueprints and schematics for anything a human colony would need to construct on-site for survival, habitation, and defense. Moreover, the AI assistance came into play especially for altering those construction templates into forms optimized for their humans' survival and tactical needs, as either an automated, or manual but incredibly user-friendly, process. And, they were designed in such a way anyone could operate one and alter schematics to fit needs, regardless of education or technical expertise.<br /> <br /> Basically, they were the equivalent of Star Trek's industrial replicators.<br /> <br /> All human colonies and colony ships were equipped with one or more STC's. But, in the few dozen millennia since, they were almost all lost, destroyed, or broke down over time, and almost none remain intact and operational. But, even finding a defunct STC is a Big Fucking Deal, since their databases may be intact and containing their original, or even updated, schematics that can be replicated and uploaded to other, functional, STC's.]</i><br /> <br /> Hence why those righteously zealous self-driving vehicles are those that come exclusively from STC's, why the AM has such a hard-on for nobody but themselves having STC access, and why STC vehicles are &quot;holier&quot; than non-STC vehicles or refurbs. (Genuine) Baneblades and Land Raiders being the &quot;smoking gun&quot;, as they can only be produced via STC and are the ones most notorious for continuing to operate after their crews were killed.<br /> <br /> No, the only god or spirit humanity is memeing into existence -- and even then, it's the human psykers being sacrificed by the millions, not the run of the mill evolved monkey -- is the fetal fifth Chaos God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 04-02-2018, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T08:29:27-07:00","id":1202228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202220#post1202220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going on about something that's going to happen in -- worst estimate -- four billion years*...is this an April Fool's post?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope, it's not an April Fool's post. The fact that this won't take place for billions of years doesn't change the fact that it will eventually happen. And if humanity isn't ready to colonize the stars by the time that happens, then the Technocracy have pretty much screwed us over.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, if their goal is to stabilize humanity towards a bright new future, then they might want to take a look at Tesla's plan to supply free power for the whole world. Which, by the way, he was actually on the cusp of doing until some jack ass slapped him with a lawsuit and that's why you have to pay electrical bills, now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T09:55:44-07:00","id":1202248,"title":"","content":"People don't believe in rockets anymore.<br /> Will the technocracy say that rockets attract technical hazards ? No. Instead, they announce stupid mistakes being made.. like ..<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://arstechnica.com/science/2017/11/this-weeks-failed-russian-rocket-had-a-pretty-bad-programming-error/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn.arstechnica.net/wp-content/uploads/2017/11/GettyImages-881810704-1024x648.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://arstechnica.com/science/2017/11/this-weeks-failed-russian-rocket-had-a-pretty-bad-programming-error/\" target=\"_blank\"> This week&rsquo;s failed Russian rocket had a pretty bad programming error </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://arstechnica.com/science/2017/11/this-weeks-failed-russian-rocket-had-a-pretty-bad-programming-error/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://arstechnica.com/science/2017/11/this-weeks-failed-russian-rocket-had-a-pretty-bad-programming-error/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Fregat upper stage sent its satellites back into Earth's atmosphere. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars_Climate_Orbiter#Cause_of_failure\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Mars_Climate_Orbiter_2.jpg/1280px-Mars_Climate_Orbiter_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars_Climate_Orbiter#Cause_of_failure\" target=\"_blank\"> Mars Climate Orbiter - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars_Climate_Orbiter#Cause_of_failure\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars_Climate_Orbiter#Cause_of_failure </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I am deeply thinking that in the age of information, such issues *CANNOT* happen. And i kindly send my disbelief to the union.<br /> <br /> To be honest, i believe that the union is stuck into the rigid consensus, like the traditions are. The advantage they had - having people trusting in science - is leaving them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T14:35:53-07:00","id":1202306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202228#post1202228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, it's not an April Fool's post. The fact that this won't take place for billions of years doesn't change the fact that it will eventually happen. And if humanity isn't ready to colonize the stars by the time that happens, then the Technocracy have pretty much screwed us over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right now I wouldn't even dare to make an accurate guess about our technology in the range of the next ~50 years. And only careful guesses in the range of 20. And that's in real life, not Mage.<br /> To give a 50 year reference, 50 years ago (just about) we haven't had anybody on the moon just yet, and the power consumers carry inside their pocket today absolutely *destroys* what costed over a million dollars back then and filled an entire room.<br /> <br /> That's 50 years in actual RL tech. Just 50.<br /> And the pace has been picking up with every decade passing during that time, and technically is only held back in some areas and boosted in others by for-profit considerations.<br /> <br /> Nobody of us can even imagine what we will have in 1000. Not even remotely. Just absolutely not.<br /> Billions of years, in that perspective, is utterly unfathomable and absurd to even consider. Homo Sapiens, in its entirety, has only existed for 300k years. That's 0.03% of just a billion years. And the vast majority of that timespan was spent hunting things with spears.<br /> <br /> If we add Mage to the mix now, I really, absolutely am not worried about Sol going supernova. I'm not worried about it in RL when it comes to humanity's survival being stopped by *that*, of all things (contrary to us just wasting the planet), and that's without magick in the mix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-02-2018, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T15:32:17-07:00","id":1202318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202306#post1202306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right now I wouldn't even dare to make an accurate guess about our technology in the range of the next ~50 years. And only careful guesses in the range of 20. And that's in real life, not Mage.<br /> To give a 50 year reference, 50 years ago (just about) we haven't had anybody on the moon just yet, and the power consumers carry inside their pocket today absolutely *destroys* what costed over a million dollars back then and filled an entire room.<br /> <br /> That's 50 years in actual RL tech. Just 50.<br /> And the pace has been picking up with every decade passing during that time, and technically is only held back in some areas and boosted in others by for-profit considerations.<br /> <br /> Nobody of us can even imagine what we will have in 1000. Not even remotely. Just absolutely not.<br /> Billions of years, in that perspective, is utterly unfathomable and absurd to even consider. Homo Sapiens, in its entirety, has only existed for 300k years. That's 0.03% of just a billion years. And the vast majority of that timespan was spent hunting things with spears.<br /> <br /> If we add Mage to the mix now, I really, absolutely am not worried about Sol going supernova. I'm not worried about it in RL when it comes to humanity's survival being stopped by *that*, of all things (contrary to us just wasting the planet), and that's without magick in the mix.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I understand what you're trying to say in regards to how rapidly we've advanced. It was less than a century between the first working flying machines, to when we were successfully launching people into outer space. Frankly, I think that 3D printers are some Star Trek level shit as it is.<br /> <br /> However, at this point in our history, we've scientifically proven that any means of colonizing the distant stars is the work of fiction. Biology, physics and general consumption of resources simply do not allow us to do so in any sort of convenient way. If the Technocracy wants to put us in space, they're going to have to change the way we perceive these limitations, not just whip up some kind of technology that miraculously fixes the problem. Because as far as I'm concerned, anything that defies scientific explanation is considered magic. And if somebody told me they invented an engine that could get me from earth, to the other side of the Milky Way in just three weeks, my response would be &quot;witchcraft!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's say for the sake of argument that they harness the power of Mass Effect, allowing us to change the mass of the ship during flight in order to achieve FTL speeds. How exactly can we travel faster than light without being crushed into pancakes against the side of the hull? It's called G-Force, and even going close to the speed of sound can cause people to black out. There's also the fact that increasing the object's mass would likewise increase its density. And when you try to create too much density, you get a black hole.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And on another topic regarding our rapid advancement in technology. You're forgetting that every time humanity has made significant leaps in progress, we have always found a way to turn that progress into a weapon and then we aim that weapon directly at ourselves. If this is the Technocracy's way of protecting our species, then I am not impressed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lastly, if the Technocracy's end goal really had our best interest at heart, then why are they the antagonists of Mage, rather than being the protagonists? Shouldn't the enemy be the Mages who want to go galavanting around with forces that want to ruin our day? Remember, the World of Darkness is supposed to be a darker, more depressing version of our reality, which means that it's very unlikely that a group as powerful as the Technocracy are doing their thing in the interest of humanitarian ideals. They have ulterior motives, and it probably involves using us as sacrificial pawns of some kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T15:50:12-07:00","id":1202320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202318#post1202318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lastly, if the Technocracy's end goal really had our best interest at heart, then why are they the antagonists of Mage, rather than being the protagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Phil, thankfully, has softened his stance a bit on the Technocracy being the &quot;bad guys.&quot; At least, he has in recent years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T17:02:14-07:00","id":1202345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202318#post1202318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, if the Technocracy's end goal really had our best interest at heart, then why are they the antagonists of Mage, rather than being the protagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be because MtAs, like every other WW product, was very much a product of the 1990s and its edgelord, GRIMDARK, &quot;fight the man!&quot; sensibility. Since, the product has evolved, much for the better, to involve shades-of-grey factions fighting for what they believe to be right, with nobody having the complete picture and being worse off for it, as opposed to heroes-by-authorial-fiat fighting villains-by-authorial-fiat.<br /> <br /> It should tell you something WW had to play up the Technocracy to moustache-twirling, Oliver Stone movie, Dick Dastardly/Snidely Whiplash, <i>ludicrously</i> over-the-top caricature levels involving grey aliens, MKULTRA, <i>literal goddamn Terminators</i>, and every other &quot;bad guy/black hat&quot; sci-fi/fantasy trope in the book, before players would even come close to buying they were antagonists in any way, shape, or form. Especially coming off the fact Ruby Ridge and Waco happened right when MtAs got released, and anyone the least bit politically-aware read the Traditions' write-up damn well should have said to themselves, &quot;these Randy Weaver, David Koresh, Jim Jones motherfuckers are supposed to be the <i>good guys</i>?&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, I love MtAs -- <b><i>now</i></b> -- as much as anyone else who visits these forums. Still doesn't change the fact when the game was released, I read it and asked myself those same questions, and came to the conclusion it was so goddamn stupid it wasn't worth touching. And I didn't, until Revised edition came along and grew the game up a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 04-02-2018, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T17:22:17-07:00","id":1202366,"title":"","content":"A case could be made that all &quot;Mages&quot; are reality warping monsters straight out of the that Star Trek episode where Kirk has to bash in the head of the guy ascending to godhood. From the perspective of humans they are all just monsters, no matter what philosophy/religion they warp reality in the name of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T18:57:56-07:00","id":1202399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202345#post1202345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be because MtAs, like every other WW product, was very much a product of the 1990s and its edgelord, GRIMDARK, &quot;fight the man!&quot; sensibility. Since, the product has evolved, much for the better, to involve shades-of-grey factions fighting for what they believe to be right, with nobody having the complete picture and being worse off for it, as opposed to heroes-by-authorial-fiat fighting villains-by-authorial-fiat.<br /> <br /> It should tell you something WW had to play up the Technocracy to moustache-twirling, Oliver Stone movie, Dick Dastardly/Snidely Whiplash, <i>ludicrously</i> over-the-top caricature levels involving grey aliens, MKULTRA, <i>literal goddamn Terminators</i>, and every other &quot;bad guy/black hat&quot; sci-fi/fantasy trope in the book, before players would even come close to buying they were antagonists in any way, shape, or form. Especially coming off the fact Ruby Ridge and Waco happened right when MtAs got released, and anyone the least bit politically-aware read the Traditions' write-up damn well should have said to themselves, &quot;these Randy Weaver, David Koresh, Jim Jones motherfuckers are supposed to be the <i>good guys</i>?&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, I love MtAs -- <b><i>now</i></b> -- as much as anyone else who visits these forums. Still doesn't change the fact when the game was released, I read it and asked myself those same questions, and came to the conclusion it was so goddamn stupid it wasn't worth touching. And I didn't, until Revised edition came along and grew the game up a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much this. I'm glad someone else made this argument, because it means I don't have to type the whole thing out (and frankly, that sounds exhausting. :P)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T20:04:16-07:00","id":1202413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202318#post1202318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, if the Technocracy's end goal really had our best interest at heart, then why are they the antagonists of Mage, rather than being the protagonists? .</div> </div> </div> </div>No not really. The Road to Hell is paved with good Intentions exists for a reason. It makes a Darker view of the technocracy all the more frightening. I Mean watch Serenity to get a &quot;person who believes in a righteous cause&quot; doing the most horrific acts. A Technocracy that just doesn't give a fuck and is in it for power is much less scary. Corrupt and weak people are much easier to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T20:34:40-07:00","id":1202423,"title":"","content":"So how does Technocracy science still Doom humanity? Colonizing the stars is doable even without magic hacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T22:34:48-07:00","id":1202458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202423#post1202423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how does Technocracy science still Doom humanity? Colonizing the stars is doable even without magic hacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, while it might be possible *purely technically* to colonize distant systems in RL right now, it would also involve<br /> <br /> 1) An insane sum of money.<br /> 2) An insane amount of planning.<br /> 3) People willing to go on a voyage that they, and a whole pile of next generations of their offspring, won't see the end of.<br /> 4) Trusting *those* generations to actually do the job down the line, which requires them properly preparing each that follows, along with upkeep of the vessel and self-sufficiency. Those generations would need to be trained and raised for that one very purpose, not with the mindset of &quot;I will give my offspring a happy life full of choices!&quot;. Because that generation and each that follows will only exist to maintain the vessel and prepare the next generation.<br /> 5) Hoping that all those generations will actually be able to handle anything like normal gravity, among things, because we have absolutely nothing like a human actually born in those conditions right now; And the effects on the physiology could be immense, starting with bones and the heart not growing to handle proper gravity.<br /> 6) Hoping that any repairs in this timespan necessary will not actually make the rest of the journey impossible, because there is no simple turning back. We already have a problem of modern computer systems being currently affected way too much by interstellar radiation, which is why so many computers up there are quite old models.<br /> 7) Hoping that supplies last, even with the ton of recycling, re-use and potentially necessary growth of food involved.<br /> 8) The will to do something like this, knowing that *we* on Earth also would (maybe) get to know the result of this whole endaevor only a whole pile of generations later, if we don't simply forget about it.<br /> 9) The pretty sure knowledge that the humans that might manage to colonize over there have as much in common with us as any society that, for hundreds of years, was separate and isolated from us.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> EDIT-BONUS:<br /> Also, since it's such a long trip, we would have to make the choice what technology we would pass along, including exact descriptions of how it works and how to build it, along with the principles behind it. As well as anything cultural we want to give them. And all of it would definitely need paper form along with multiple digital copies.<br /> <br /> Because those that would maaaaaaaaaybe manage to arrive there, and then maaaaaaaybe colonize there won't be able to reproduce multiple key technologies that are standard for us. For a long time. Like..well. Computers. Those that they have on arrival would be priceless artifacts.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <br /> So. It might be, in theory, technologically possible right now. But the way we would have to do it, *right now*, gives us absolutely zero reason to do so and would be an incredible risk and investment, to make a big understatement. All with a very very very high chance of &quot;Well, never heard of 'em again&quot;.<br /> <br /> Let's try Mars first. That's already a trip with incredible hardships for generations to come after arrival, if we ever plan to colonize, and many chances for things to horribly go wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-03-2018, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T04:54:24-07:00","id":1202525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202458#post1202458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, while it might be possible *purely technically* to colonize distant systems in RL right now, it would also involve<br /> <br /> *snip*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Such is the basis of my argument. Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T06:53:43-07:00","id":1202543,"title":"","content":"Frankly I think we should work on genetic engineering before we try to colonize deep space. Remake humanity into something that could safely survive the trip. Or replace these collection-of-water-baloon bodies entirely with machines. Post genetic and/or AI singularities, space travel becomes a much easier problem to solve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:29:48-07:00","id":1202563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202543#post1202543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly I think we should work on genetic engineering before we try to colonize deep space. Remake humanity into something that could safely survive the trip. Or replace these collection-of-water-baloon bodies entirely with machines. Post genetic and/or AI singularities, space travel becomes a much easier problem to solve.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Funny you should bring that up, since we've performed DNA tests on astronauts who returned from space and found their DNA had been altered from what it was before they left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:56:53-07:00","id":1202586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand what you're trying to say in regards to how rapidly we've advanced. It was less than a century between the first working flying machines, to when we were successfully launching people into outer space. Frankly, I think that 3D printers are some Star Trek level shit as it is.<br /> <br /> However, at this point in our history, we've scientifically proven that any means of colonizing the distant stars is the work of fiction. Biology, physics and general consumption of resources simply do not allow us to do so in any sort of convenient way. If the Technocracy wants to put us in space, they're going to have to change the way we perceive these limitations, not just whip up some kind of technology that miraculously fixes the problem. Because as far as I'm concerned, anything that defies scientific explanation is considered magic. And if somebody told me they invented an engine that could get me from earth, to the other side of the Milky Way in just three weeks, my response would be &quot;witchcraft!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Since we have billions of years (more than the whole human history) and science has made several paradigm shifts since the beginning of modern age a few centuries ago (Remember when developing working lasers was deemed impossible or a tremedous waste of energy? the realm of fancy sci-fy? Because that was like 70 years ago).I think it's safe to assume that caring about the sun exploding it's not a priority.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's say for the sake of argument that they harness the power of Mass Effect, allowing us to change the mass of the ship during flight in order to achieve FTL speeds. How exactly can we travel faster than light without being crushed into pancakes against the side of the hull? It's called G-Force, and even going close to the speed of sound can cause people to black out. There's also the fact that increasing the object's mass would likewise increase its density. And when you try to create too much density, you get a black hole. </div> </div> </div>As you can see, Sci-Fi has evolved since the time Jules Verne wrote about flying machines and rockets. If science keeps evolving at it's current rate, our current sci-fi may end looking just as outdated in a few centuries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And on another topic regarding our rapid advancement in technology. You're forgetting that every time humanity has made significant leaps in progress, we have always found a way to turn that progress into a weapon and then we aim that weapon directly at ourselves. If this is the Technocracy's way of protecting our species, then I am not impressed. </div> </div> </div>And the solution it's not to progress?. Traditions are divided in this regards, while OoH would have humanity take a longer road to progress Etherites already wanted space colonization and free energy (and the superweapons such technology would give us) before the 2nd World War. Technocracy takes a middle ground.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastly, if the Technocracy's end goal really had our best interest at heart, then why are they the antagonists of Mage, rather than being the protagonists? Shouldn't the enemy be the Mages who want to go galavanting around with forces that want to ruin our day? </div> </div> </div>This has been adressed, but to add remember that Technocracy are *the* Mage Hunters. Even if they were saints (which they most certainly are not) they would be your main concern if you were a Mage (and not one of them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember, the World of Darkness is supposed to be a darker, more depressing version of our reality, which means that it's very unlikely that a group as powerful as the Technocracy are doing their thing in the interest of humanitarian ideals. They have ulterior motives, and it probably involves using us as sacrificial pawns of some kind. </div> </div> </div>Oh, they're very idealistic but very corrupt. Power corrupts and all that. They don't want humanity as sacrificial pawns, they want to control humanity as an enlightened elite. They want humanity to remain safe and cozy under their boots. For our own good, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-03-2018, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T09:13:39-07:00","id":1202616,"title":"","content":"We can see pretty clearly in real life that tribalism is the biggest corrupter and danger to the modern world, not genuine fanatics for evil ideals, which are extraordinarily rare. Tribalism corrupt capitalism into crony-capitalism, because the first winners of the capitalist competition favor their family and golfing buddies, gradually accumulating more power, squelching competition, and creating a de facto oligarchy. Tribalism corrupts communism into Stalinism and near-Stalinism because those bureaucrats in charge of distributing the wealth favor their families and golfing buddies, need more and more power to protect the position that allows them to do this, and this spirals into a bureaucratic oligarchy. Tribalism corrupts democracy into demagoguery because people vote to favor the visible short-term interests of themselves, their families, and their friends over a more educated and nuanced view that takes the interests of humanity as a whole into account rather than the immediately visible tribe. <br /> <br /> Never blame fanatical ideals when tribalism is the simpler answer. Tribalism and pragmatic nihilism are the most consistent predictors of human behavior on a macro-scale.<br /> <br /> Technocrats care about technocrats. They care about their own power and wealth and the power and wealth of their friends and families. Other groups threaten that, either directly or by offering humanity other choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T10:41:29-07:00","id":1202648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202413#post1202413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Technocracy that just doesn't give a fuck and is in it for power is much less scary. Corrupt and weak people are much easier to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you equating that a Mage (or a group of Mages) who is &quot;being in for power&quot; is also&quot;corrupt&quot; and &quot;weak&quot; ? If yes, then could you explain why do you think it is so ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-03-2018, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:01:22-07:00","id":1202752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202318#post1202318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I understand what you're trying to say in regards to how rapidly we've advanced. It was less than a century between the first working flying machines, to when we were successfully launching people into outer space. Frankly, I think that 3D printers are some Star Trek level shit as it is.<br /> <br /> However, at this point in our history, we've scientifically proven that any means of colonizing the distant stars is the work of fiction. Biology, physics and general consumption of resources simply do not allow us to do so in any sort of convenient way. If the Technocracy wants to put us in space, they're going to have to change the way we perceive these limitations, not just whip up some kind of technology that miraculously fixes the problem. Because as far as I'm concerned, anything that defies scientific explanation is considered magic. And if somebody told me they invented an engine that could get me from earth, to the other side of the Milky Way in just three weeks, my response would be &quot;witchcraft!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's say for the sake of argument that they harness the power of Mass Effect, allowing us to change the mass of the ship during flight in order to achieve FTL speeds. How exactly can we travel faster than light without being crushed into pancakes against the side of the hull? It's called G-Force, and even going close to the speed of sound can cause people to black out. There's also the fact that increasing the object's mass would likewise increase its density. And when you try to create too much density, you get a black hole.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And on another topic regarding our rapid advancement in technology. You're forgetting that every time humanity has made significant leaps in progress, we have always found a way to turn that progress into a weapon and then we aim that weapon directly at ourselves. If this is the Technocracy's way of protecting our species, then I am not impressed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lastly, if the Technocracy's end goal really had our best interest at heart, then why are they the antagonists of Mage, rather than being the protagonists? Shouldn't the enemy be the Mages who want to go galavanting around with forces that want to ruin our day? Remember, the World of Darkness is supposed to be a darker, more depressing version of our reality, which means that it's very unlikely that a group as powerful as the Technocracy are doing their thing in the interest of humanitarian ideals. They have ulterior motives, and it probably involves using us as sacrificial pawns of some kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is simple. Those rules are wrong. The Technocracy will perform, and publicize, experiments proving as such when they believe the masses are ready for such technology. Everything you know about science is a lie. Everything you know about science is well argued bullshit. The world does not actually run by rules, and as the Technocracy writes the laws of physics they can re-write them more or less as needed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:37:39-07:00","id":1202765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202586#post1202586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> And the solution it's not to progress?. Traditions are divided in this regards, while OoH would have humanity take a longer road to progress Etherites already wanted space colonization and free energy (and the superweapons such technology would give us) before the 2nd World War. Technocracy takes a middle ground.<br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, my solution is to get rid of the Technocracy so we can find other alternatives forward.<br /> <br /> And my point wasn't the fact that our tech is dangerous. The point was that if humanity keeps going the way it has been for the last 300,000 years, then we are eventually going to reach a point in which we wipe ourselves out fighting over our dwindling resources, or we completely stagnate because the Technocracy decides &quot;Yeah, okay, this is getting too dangerous.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Scientist:</b> I've done it, I've created a machine that can fully synthesize organic material. We'll never go hungry again!<br /> <br /> <b>Military Contractor:</b> Excellent! We can use this technology to synthesize bio weapons on site!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T20:41:02-07:00","id":1202856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202648#post1202648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you equating that a Mage (or a group of Mages) who is &quot;being in for power&quot; is also&quot;corrupt&quot; and &quot;weak&quot; ? If yes, then could you explain why do you think it is so ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the narrative of &quot;we are going to make you better and you have no choice to be in our experiments&quot; far more scary from the perspective as a player than &quot;the technocracy is just corrupt and mean&quot; An Order of Reason that said &quot;we have to kill off 9/10s of the Native AMerican population for the Greater Good of Humanity&quot; and meant it is far more frightening to me than &quot;well we did it by accident..&quot;<br /> <br /> That they have all these wonders that from their perspective easily justifies breaking afew eggs, unfortunately you play those eggs. Its the horror of Utilitarianism taken to the extreme, That to me is a far more interesting, a far more frightening Technocracy as an anatogonist than &quot;Mean people who just run the world&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T21:03:48-07:00","id":1202862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202765#post1202765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Scientist:</b> I've done it, I've created a machine that can fully synthesize organic material. We'll never go hungry again!<br /> <br /> <b>Military Contractor:</b> Excellent! We can use this technology to synthesize bio weapons on site!</div> </div> </div> </div>To be 'fair', our biggest overall boosts in technology in the last centuries went the other way around <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Military:</b> World War (insert number here) is over! We poured our resources recklessy into boosting / developing these technologies without economical thought.<br /> <b>Scientists:</b> Oh, this is very interesting. if you look at this, we can use it for all kinds of civilian use and develop it further!<br /> <br /> As sad as it is, many of our modern transportation technologies, computers and even space flight essentially came from those insane spendings, as well as the post-WW Cold War desire to have the bigger political you-know-what.<br /> Not that this makes such a conflict ever desirable again, but..yeah. That's sadly how it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T21:29:12-07:00","id":1202866,"title":"","content":"So, the only options we're entertaining here are variations on the Technocracy as bad guys? Because one of the best features of M20 (and the MRev Convention Books) as far as I'm concerned is the way the Technocracy is portrayed in a more positive light. Yes, they have their failings, just like everyone else; but they also have enough redeeming qualities that you can play them straight without having to play them as villains. And while it's true that Technocrats tend to have antagonistic relations with other mages, they don't always: the Syndicate and the Void Engineers, in particular, can and do work with the Traditions fairly regularly. <br /> <br /> Speaking of the Void Engineers: they're the ones who introduced Tychoidean Cosmology, a major aspect of which is \u201cConventional Space obeys Einstein's theories of Relativity, and our goal is to extend Conventional Space as far as possible in order to keep the aliens as far from Earth as possible\u201d. Remember, Mage's cosmology is not <i>our</i> cosmology: Conventional Space does not extend indefinitely; only up to the Spatial Horizon (which, admittedly, the VEs are doing their best to push as far away from Earth as possible). And it's paired with Subspace<sup><span style=\"font-size:8px\">\u2605</span></sup>, an extra-dimensional region that can be used as a shortcut to bypass Conventional Space if needed. It's not in the Consensus (yet?) because the VEs haven't successfully sanitized it. But one day, when it can be made safe for Sleepers, it <i>will</i> be introduced to the Consensus; and the Masses will be able to go to the stars (which, by then, will hopefully be within the Spatial Horizon). <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> \u2605 Subspace is called \u201cEtherspace\u201d by the Etherites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T22:06:46-07:00","id":1202867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202866#post1202866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the only options we're entertaining here are variations on the Technocracy as bad guys? Because one of the best features of M20 (and the MRev Convention Books) as far as I'm concerned is the way the Technocracy is portrayed in a more positive light. Yes, they have their failings, just like everyone else; but they also have enough redeeming qualities that you can play them straight without having to play them as villains. And while it's true that Technocrats tend to have antagonistic relations with other mages, they don't always: the Syndicate and the Void Engineers, in particular, can and do work with the Traditions fairly regularly.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't accept that the methodology the Technocracy uses justifies itself. But this is purely from an omniscient out of universe perspective. That is to say I have trouble accepting the &quot;conspiracy that hides the majority of the universe from people because 'they aren't ready&quot; are good guys.<br /> <br /> But when I get into THEIR mindset I can see how they are heroic faction. I don't feel I need to change things to get into their mindset as the protectors of the world in the face of all sorts of horrors.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T22:35:29-07:00","id":1202871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202867#post1202867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't accept that the methodology the Technocracy uses justifies itself. But this is purely from an omniscient out of universe perspective. That is to say I have trouble accepting the &quot;conspiracy that hides the majority of the universe from people because 'they aren't ready&quot; are good guys.<br /> <br /> But when I get into THEIR mindset I can see how they are heroic faction. I don't feel I need to change things to get into their mindset as the protectors of the world in the face of all sorts of horrors.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is exactly the shades-of-grey angle that Mage has been pushing since revised; Everybody thinks they are, in a way, the good guys. Which is, really, how things tend to go in RL.<br /> And all of them, from their point of view, are correct. If you pull away from their point of view and look at things objectively, the perspective changes and you begin to see the flaws.<br /> <br /> And it is, usually, very hard to look at things objectively if you are heavily invested into something for a long, long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T22:45:31-07:00","id":1202875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202871#post1202871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that is exactly the shades-of-grey angle that Mage has been pushing since revised; Everybody thinks they are, in a way, the good guys. Which is, really, how things tend to go in RL.<br /> And all of them, from their point of view, are correct. If you pull away from their point of view and look at things objectively, the perspective changes and you begin to see the flaws.<br /> <br /> And it is, usually, very hard to look at things objectively if you are heavily invested into something for a long, long time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's not how I'd use shades of grey. I think the Technocracy are the bad guys, but they are the bad guys like the Operative in Serenity. They legitimately want to make the world a better place. I think this makes the BETTER villains than the more one dimentional &quot;I got mine fuck you&quot; 1e view(Not that there isn't room for corruption in the Technocracy). I don't believe from the perspective of someone who is completely outside the system that they are right, I as a person don't feel they have an equally valid point with the information I know from an omniscient ooc perspective.<br /> <br /> However I see how they got there, and feel they got their legitimately even if its the wrong place to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T23:39:47-07:00","id":1202884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202875#post1202875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe from the perspective of someone who is completely outside the system that they are right, I as a person don't feel they have an equally valid point with the information I know from an omniscient ooc perspective.<br /> <br /> However I see how they got there, and feel they got their legitimately even if its the wrong place to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but you'll equally find people on these forums that go 'The Technocracy are the good guys' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> So it's even a matter of opinion from the outside point of view. I think the overall consensus (heh) is though that none of the factions are completely wrong or completely right. Just the amount of wrong and right shifts from Mage player to Mage player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T00:03:30-07:00","id":1202886,"title":"","content":"More to the point: whether any given faction is the good guys or the bad guys is deliberately left up to the Storyteller to decide (with the notable exception of the Nephandi, where the books stated position is &quot;we can't stop you from playing these guys if you want to; but if you want to, we suggest seeking psychological help.&quot;)<br /> <br /> This is not how it was in earlier editions of the game. From 1e to Revised, the base assumption was that the protagonists hail from the Traditions, and that the Technocracy was the most visible antagonist. M20 abandoned that when it presented the Traditions, Technocracy, and Disparates all as viable protagonists in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-04-2018, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T00:52:20-07:00","id":1202898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202886#post1202886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From 1e to Revised, the base assumption was that the protagonists hail from the Traditions, and that the Technocracy was the most visible antagonist. M20 abandoned that when it presented the Traditions, Technocracy, and Disparates all as viable protagonists in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yup. M20 is the first corebook to make them equal choices, though as a generally viable protagonistic option, It started with...<i>Guide To The Technocracy</i>, I think? Which, unless i'm mistaken, was the last book to appear before Revised Core.<br /> They *would* probably have gotten into Revised core as an equal choice if Brucato stil had his hands on the development by Revised core, but alas.<br /> Then again, the grimdark of Revised made the Traditions the most logical choice as the protagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T01:50:28-07:00","id":1202913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202886#post1202886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More to the point: whether any given faction is the good guys or the bad guys is deliberately left up to the Storyteller to decide (with the notable exception of the Nephandi, where the books stated position is &quot;we can't stop you from playing these guys if you want to; but if you want to, we suggest seeking psychological help.&quot;)<br /> <br /> This is not how it was in earlier editions of the game. From 1e to Revised, the base assumption was that the protagonists hail from the Traditions, and that the Technocracy was the most visible antagonist. M20 abandoned that when it presented the Traditions, Technocracy, and Disparates all as viable protagonists in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I Profoundly disagree. While the Technocracy are presented as a playable option. I would say they are Presented as the Default bad guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T02:20:22-07:00","id":1202918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202898#post1202898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yup. M20 is the first corebook to make them equal choices, though as a generally viable protagonistic option, It started with...<i>Guide To The Technocracy</i>, I think? Which, unless i'm mistaken, was the last book to appear before Revised Core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The 1e Technocrat books have lots of player stuff, whilst Book of Chantries has story seeds based on being a Technocrat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T02:35:03-07:00","id":1202920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202913#post1202913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I Profoundly disagree. While the Technocracy are presented as a playable option. I would say they are Presented as the Default bad guys.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I consider them villains for the same reason that Changeling considers the Dauntain to be villains. The Technocracy are mages who fear / hate everything magical about the universe and want to eliminate it. That's like playing an adventurer who wants to rid the world of all quest givers!<br /> <br /> <br /> I do not consider human life to be inherently more valuable than any of the other sentient races / creatures who exist in World of Darkness, especially not when human history proves it can be just as corrupt as they can. It's also due to that point of view that I'm so easily comfortable playing the more controversial type characters in these games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They also have zero regard for the beliefs and traditions of other cultures and seek to force feed their way of thinking down your throat. </span></span></span>In that regard, the Technocracy can be described <b>at best</b> as being a group of genocidal maniacs who won't rest until they've stamped out everything they perceive as being a threat to their goal of human supremacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-04-2018, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T08:44:33-07:00","id":1203023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202920#post1202920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I consider them villains for the same reason that Changeling considers the Dauntain to be villains. The Technocracy are mages who fear / hate everything magical about the universe and want to eliminate it. That's like playing an adventurer who wants to rid the world of all quest givers!</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's like playing an adventurer that wants to get rid of all the dragons and undead and evil wizards that threaten his hometown. Y'know. Like an adventurer. The Technocracy doesn't want to get rid of imagination and wonder, they want to harness it in a way that allows it to do as little damage as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202920#post1202920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not consider human life to be inherently more valuable than any of the other sentient races / creatures who exist in World of Darkness, especially not when human history proves it can be just as corrupt as they can. It's also due to that point of view that I'm so easily comfortable playing the more controversial type characters in these games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's go down the list of other sentient beings in the WoD, shall we?<ul><li><b>Vampires - </b>Need humanity in order to continue existing. (And the Technocracy isn't really opposed to them.)</li> <li><b>Fera - </b>Need humanity in order to continue existing.</li> <li><b>Changelings - </b>Need humanity and the Technocrats aren't actively trying to kill them or even know they exist.</li> <li><b>Wraiths - </b>Need humanity. Can only exist within the context of humanity.</li> <li><b>Spirits - </b>They'll be fine. There's exactly 0 chance that spirits will go extinct or that their quality of life will get meaningfully worse.</li> <li><b>Mummies </b>- Basically are humans.</li> <li><b>Hunters - </b>Basically are humans.</li> <li><b>Demons - </b>Need humanity or they would be Earthbound.</li> <li><b>Aliens - </b>The ones not in league with the Nephandi almost never encounter humans.</li> <li><b>Dragon Kings</b> - Extinct.</li> </ul>Did I miss any?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202920#post1202920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also have zero regard for the beliefs and traditions of other cultures and seek to force feed their way of thinking down your throat. In that regard, the Technocracy can be described <b>at best</b> as being a group of genocidal maniacs who won't rest until they've stamped out everything they perceive as being a threat to their goal of human supremacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you actually imagine a reality where objective truth was not a thing? A world where every culture's internalized narrative of inherent superiority was, for all intents and purposes, an objective cosmic truth? Can you imagine a world where the sun actually didn't rise in the morning unless you made a human sacrifice every equinox? Where holy wars and inquisitions were actually given with divine approval? Can you imagine a world where the only real source of power is the single-minded, fanatical belief that you are objectively correct about everything?<br /> <br /> Peace and cross-cultural tolerance are impossible when you're all playing by different rules on every level of reality.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy wants to give the world a <i>lingua franca</i>. They're trying to create a level playing field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T08:57:01-07:00","id":1203028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202913#post1202913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I Profoundly disagree. While the Technocracy are presented as a playable option. I would say they are Presented as the Default bad guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Objectively, in M20? No. <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times New Roman\">Unlike previous editions of <b>Mage</b> (aside from <b>Sorcerers Crusade</b>), <b>Mage 20</b> does not default to a Traditions-centric viewpoint. Instead, we're presenting a wide range of potential <b>Mage</b> characters. With that range comes a bigger perspective on the Awakened experience, so the following chapter features as objective a view as you could possibly get from a world in which reality is anything but certain.</span><br /> \u2014 page 120</div>The chapter in question covers Awakened history and the various factions of the Ascension War. But the even-handed approach isn't confined to that chapter: throughout the book, you have statements like \u201cmystic mages blame the Technocracy, the Technocrats blame the mystics, and both sides of that divide are right.\u201d (p.75) <br /> <br /> See also the Common Ground section on pp.349\u2013353, which includes several examples of how a troupe including both Technocrats and non-Technocrats can be brought together and given enough rationale to stay together to hold a chronicle together. Chapter Seven ends with summaries of five types of Chronicles: the Traditions, the Technocracy, the Disparates, the Orphans, and the Mixed-Faction. <br /> <br /> The closest M20 comes to an anti-Technocrat bias is the way it occasionally presents Technocratic terminology off to the side, and tends to use the Traditions' terminology by default. But that's more a case of practicality than bias. <br /> <br /> You're free to choose to see the Technocracy as the bad guys; but that's <i>your choice,</i> not something M20 pushes on you. You might even decide that the Technocracy is objectively bad, and that anyone who sees them as the good guys is delusional. M20 actively warns <i>against</i> such certainty, citing it as a symptom of hubris while indicating that it's an all-too-common flaw among mages of all stripes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-04-2018, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T09:14:50-07:00","id":1203037,"title":"","content":"Except Nyrufa you're forgetting something important, this is the <i>World of Darkness</i>. Most of those non-human beings aren't friendly and will actively abuse the Masses if given the chance. Vampires regularly feed upon and often kill mortals as well as manipulate them in their petty games of power. Mortals are regularly caught in the crossfire of the werewolves' wars. Hell, most Pentex employees are normal humans with no knowledge of what their bosses are really up to but that doesn't stop the Garou from carving through them all the same. Wraiths feed off human emotion and there are plenty that will invade the Skinlands for fun or havoc. The spirits and aliens, especially those from far beyond Earth are alien things that even Traditionalists will agree that they should be kept far from the Masses because of just how dangerous those things are.<br /> <br /> And ultimately, just as one can see the good of the Technocracy, one can see the evils of the Traditions, to see them as dangerous Reality Terrorists. Men and women so obsessed with their pursuit of Magic and Wonder that they lose sight or simply don't care about the damage they could cause to those around them. Even when they try to use their Magic to help the Masses it can lead to disastrous results.<br /> <br /> So yeah, they are pro-human and stick to their beliefs because nearly everything else they've encountered is varying degrees of dangerous. When faced with that, it's not really that hard to understand why they would eventually become what they are now. The world is a dangerous place and the Union for all it's faults and evils is trying to make it safer for the Masses which makes them one of the few major groups in WoD to have that as a principle mandate.<br /> <br /> After all, the Craftmasons and the Order of Reason were ultimately born in part because of the cruelties, excesses and hubris of Mages. And even back then, the Order wasn't all 'Burn the Witch, burn the Monsters!' Certainly there were groups within the Order that were like that but there were just as many other groups that wanted to study the Supernatural and generally wouldn't go after them unless they were dangerous.<br /> <br /> Does the Technocracy have issues? Sure it does. But personally I see less as maliciously evil and more as corrupted by victory and hubris. And that had the situation been reversed, with the Traditions becoming the dominant Mage group over the Order of Reason, I could just as easily see the Traditions becoming just as bad as the Technocracy is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T09:50:51-07:00","id":1203044,"title":"","content":"Also, don't forget the box on p.169: even if you have chosen not to go with the so-called \u201ckinder, gentler Technocracy\u201d of the Revised Convention Books, it's still a potential future for the Technocracy. The Union is not beyond reform \u2014 unless you decide that they are.<br /> <br /> I would also say that the Traditions don't get a pass just because they're the underdogs in the Traditions/Technocracy conflict: there's plenty bad about them even as they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T10:06:46-07:00","id":1203050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203023#post1203023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Can you actually imagine a reality where objective truth was not a thing? A world where every culture's internalized narrative of inherent superiority was, for all intents and purposes, an objective cosmic truth? Can you imagine a world where the sun actually didn't rise in the morning unless you made a human sacrifice every equinox? Where holy wars and inquisitions were actually given with divine approval? Can you imagine a world where the only real source of power is the single-minded, fanatical belief that you are objectively correct about everything?<br /> <br /> Peace and cross-cultural tolerance are impossible when you're all playing by different rules on every level of reality.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy wants to give the world a <i>lingua franca</i>. They're trying to create a level playing field.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually, yes, I can. <br /> <br /> 1 - I was raised in a religious household, though eventually renounced.<br /> <br /> 2 - I have always been fascinated by mythology and the occult<br /> <br /> 3 - I was a <b>true believer</b> in magic and the supernatural when I was younger.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as for the only source of power being the directly linked to the strength of your mind: That is exactly what I think of when it comes to using magic. I've often heard the story that magic operates in accordance with ancient laws and how there are some things that it can't accomplish.<br /> <br /> <br /> I reject this idea entirely. If magic is the power to warp reality (which it seems to be in Mage), and it is governed by the strength of your imagination, then that would logically mean that magic has no limitations. As long as you believe in it, it becomes possible, regardless of the general consensus is to the contrary. In laymen's terms, you dictate the rules, which are as malleable as your own interpretation of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's why for the longest time, I have considered magic and science to be different from each other. Science tries to apply rules and deductive reasoning to how things work. Magic chooses to ignore those laws and reasoning, making it beyond the realm of scientific explanation. <br /> <br /> <br /> If they want an even playing field, then the Technocracy could easily settle for using pocket dimensions, and give everybody (or at least every mage) the freedom to create their own personalized universes. That way, everyone is happy without stepping on anybody's toes.<br /> <br /> <br /> But no, they don't trust us to wield that kind of power. And if they don't trust us, then why in the hell would we trust them? Because they claim to have the vision necessary to lead us into the future? Yeah, just how many tyrannical dictators have used that exact line of reasoning to justify their own regimes? And how often did such regimes end in disaster as a result of their leader's hubris?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203023#post1203023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Let's go down the list of other sentient beings in the WoD, shall we?</span></span></span><ul><li><b>Vampires - </b>Need humanity in order to continue existing. (And the Technocracy isn't really opposed to them.)</li> <li><b>Fera - </b>Need humanity in order to continue existing.</li> <li><b>Changelings - </b>Need humanity and the Technocrats aren't actively trying to kill them or even know they exist.</li> <li><b>Wraiths - </b>Need humanity. Can only exist within the context of humanity.</li> <li><b>Spirits - </b>They'll be fine. There's exactly 0 chance that spirits will go extinct or that their quality of life will get meaningfully worse.</li> <li><b>Mummies </b>- Basically are humans.</li> <li><b>Hunters - </b>Basically are humans.</li> <li><b>Demons - </b>Need humanity or they would be Earthbound.</li> <li><b>Aliens - </b>The ones not in league with the Nephandi almost never encounter humans.</li> <li><b>Dragon Kings</b> - Extinct.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> And how many living creatures does humanity depend on in order to survive? Oh, sure, you could make the argument that plants and animals don't matter as much, because they're not intelligent enough to comprehend the grander scope of things. But that is exactly how many supernaturals who prey upon mortals would logically see humanity. More often than not, mortals only care about what is immediately applicable to their current situation or lot in life. They don't give much thought to what goes on behind the curtain until somebody forcefully peels it back for them. And when that happens, they usually freak out once they see what's going on. A lot like cattle being lead to the slaughter house, pretty much.<br /> <br /> In that regard, the supernatural creatures that we define as being &quot;monsters&quot; actually behave no differently than we humans do. They've simply been made privy to a higher state of awareness than the rest of us.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Changelings needing humanity to survive, I would argue against that by pointing to all the nobles who fled to Arcadia and remained there for many centuries while humanity continued to embrace logic and science. They didn't have any difficulty surviving until after they came back to the Autumn World. And judging by how the nobles were acting once they finally came back, it sounds like they spent their time in Arcadia doing things exactly the same as they always had, regardless of what humanity thought at the time. Also one of the possible end of the world scenarios puts forth the idea of the Fae packing it in and conducting a mass evacuation back to the Dreaming, with the members of House Danaan purifying their fae spirits using cold iron weaponry.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fera also don't explicitly need humanity, since they can just reproduce with themselves. <br /> <br /> I don't think Wraiths count for much, since nobody actually wants to be a Wraith in the first place.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T10:18:09-07:00","id":1203053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203037#post1203037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Nyrufa you're forgetting something important, this is the <i>World of Darkness</i>. Most of those non-human beings aren't friendly and will actively abuse the Masses if given the chance. Vampires regularly feed upon and often kill mortals as well as manipulate them in their petty games of power. Mortals are regularly caught in the crossfire of the werewolves' wars. Hell, most Pentex employees are normal humans with no knowledge of what their bosses are really up to but that doesn't stop the Garou from carving through them all the same. Wraiths feed off human emotion and there are plenty that will invade the Skinlands for fun or havoc. The spirits and aliens, especially those from far beyond Earth are alien things that even Traditionalists will agree that they should be kept far from the Masses because of just how dangerous those things are.<br /> <br /> And ultimately, just as one can see the good of the Technocracy, one can see the evils of the Traditions, to see them as dangerous Reality Terrorists. Men and women so obsessed with their pursuit of Magic and Wonder that they lose sight or simply don't care about the damage they could cause to those around them. Even when they try to use their Magic to help the Masses it can lead to disastrous results.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes, and humanity has often done the exact same thing to each other. I fail to see why monsters are considered any worse in that regard. Whether it's the hands of a vampire or a human being, people are still getting killed. The difference is that a vampire usually has a valid reason for killing (food, or self preservation), where as a human often does so purely out of more selfish reasons.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for calling the Traditions 'reality terrorists' I disapprove of that moniker, In fact, I think people have forgotten what terrorism actually is, since they throw the word around to describe every dangerous person these days. <b>A terrorist is somebody who uses fear as a means of controlling others.</b><br /> <br /> Wanting the freedom to practice magic the way you want to is NOT an act of terrorism. It is the desire to live your life as a free thinking individual.<br /> <br /> Shutting us off from the outside world and saying that we will be slaughtered if we ever open the door IS an act of terrorism. They're threatening us with a gruesome death as punishment for not following their rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Oh, and I just realized that we are operating under the assumption that the Technocracy is the only means of protecting us from the threat of the supernatural. As if we've suddenly forgotten that humans throughout history have believed in the use of sacred charms, wards, talismans, rituals, materials or holy sites which are meant to repel otherworldly forces.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the Technocracy didn't always exist. There was a time in history where the supernatural had a much stronger hold over mortals than it does now. And yes, while it's true that our species wasn't exactly thriving under their influence, we also weren't being driven to extinction as a result of mindless aggression. Remember, in the World of Darkness, many of these supernatural forces are sentient, and possess a level of intelligence at least somewhat comparable to humanity, if not beyond it. I'm pretty sure the majority of them would see the folly of purging the human race and try to operate in a more tactful fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-04-2018, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T10:25:17-07:00","id":1203057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202920#post1202920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also have zero regard for the beliefs and traditions of other cultures and seek to force feed their way of thinking down your throat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's much less true in M20 than it has been in the past. In fact, with M20's \u201cmake the game your own\u201d design philosophy and various Future Fates and similar options presented throughout, it's only as true in M20 as you want it to be.<br /> <br /> Personally, I suspect that when <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> finally gets published, we'll see a much more multi-cultural Technocracy. We already know from its description that it will cover the Asian and African Technocracies as well as the conventional Technocracy; and I suspect that the upcoming reorganization hinted at in M20 will end up replacing the five Eurocentric Conventions with a set of Conventions drawing from at least three culturally diverse sources.<br /> <br /> As for the so-called \u201chuman supremacist\u201d nature of the Technocracy: that's a feature of the <i>game</i>, not the <i>Union</i>. Awakened Magick is virtually unique to humans because only humans have Avatars: the only exception I've found to this are among godlike spirit entities; and even then, it's not clear if such entities work magick or \u201cmerely\u201d exercise spiritual capabilities that are sufficiently powerful to be indistinguishable from magick as far as mere mortals (including mages) are concerned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T10:34:29-07:00","id":1203058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202898#post1202898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yup. M20 is the first corebook to make them equal choices, though as a generally viable protagonistic option, It started with...<i>Guide To The Technocracy</i>, I think? Which, unless i'm mistaken, was the last book to appear before Revised Core.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Mage: the Sorcerers Crusade</b>, actually. And there <i>were</i> a couple of books published between GttTech and MRev: the \u201c___ of the Art\u201d books, in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-04-2018, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T10:54:24-07:00","id":1203066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203057#post1203057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's much less true in M20 than it has been in the past. In fact, with M20's \u201cmake the game your own\u201d design philosophy and various Future Fates and similar options presented throughout, it's only as true in M20 as you want it to be.<br /> <br /> Personally, I suspect that when <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> finally gets published, we'll see a much more multi-cultural Technocracy. We already know from its description that it will cover the Asian and African Technocracies as well as the conventional Technocracy; and I suspect that the upcoming reorganization hinted at in M20 will end up replacing the five Eurocentric Conventions with a set of Conventions drawing from at least three culturally diverse sources.<br /> <br /> As for the so-called \u201chuman supremacist\u201d nature of the Technocracy: that's a feature of the <i>game</i>, not the <i>Union</i>. Awakened Magick is virtually unique to humans because only humans have Avatars: the only exception I've found to this are among godlike spirit entities; and even then, it's not clear if such entities work magick or \u201cmerely\u201d exercise spiritual capabilities that are sufficiently powerful to be indistinguishable from magick as far as mere mortals (including mages) are concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That will be kind of difficult to imagine. Technology is technology, I don't think it adheres to any specific form of nationality. It's basically just bragging rights over which culture was responsible for inventing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> But this debate is getting out of hand. The original post wasn't a discussing on why the Technocracy did what they did. It was more about pointing out the consequences for what they did and how it impacts humanity's future going forward. Sure, to an awakened mind, the distance between Earth and that planet made out of diamond is only about 60 feet beyond Mars. But the rest of humanity believes the distance is significantly greater. It also believes that traveling that distance in a manner that is even remotely convenient is scientifically impossible.<br /> <br /> <br /> This isn't something as simple as designing the first airplane. We knew that flight was possible, we've seen many different species of animals capable of achieving flight and we modeled the airplane off their design. We have never seen anything travel faster than the speed of light, nor seen a living being frozen in ice for thousands of years and manage to survive after being thawed out. No, this kind of technology is a violation of the laws of physics and biology alike. And if the Technocracy wants us to surpass those limitations, then they're going to have to demonstrate that doing so is possible, and explain it in such a way that we can comprehend beyond equating it to the stuff of miracles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T11:06:22-07:00","id":1203070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203050#post1203050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, yes, I can.<br /> <br /> 1 - I was raised in a religious household, though eventually renounced.<br /> <br /> 2 - I have always been fascinated by mythology and the occult<br /> <br /> 3 - I was a <b>true believer</b> in magic and the supernatural when I was younger.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as for the only source of power being the directly linked to the strength of your mind: That is exactly what I think of when it comes to using magic. I've often heard the story that magic operates in accordance with ancient laws and how there are some things that it can't accomplish.<br /> <br /> <br /> I reject this idea entirely. If magic is the power to warp reality (which it seems to be in Mage), and it is governed by the strength of your imagination, then that would logically mean that magic has no limitations. As long as you believe in it, it becomes possible, regardless of the general consensus is to the contrary. In laymen's terms, you dictate the rules, which are as malleable as your own interpretation of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not how it is in Mage: the Ascension. There are concrete laws of Reality created by the Consensus. That's why Reality works as it does. Magic, Enlightened Science, Willworking, whatever you wish to call it, is the bending or breaking of those laws to achieve something. And only the Awakened can truly do individually. For the Sleepers it is simply their collective subconscious will working together to establish the laws of the Consensus.<br /> <br /> Sure, you can get groups of Sleepers to agree on things contrary to those laws and create a bubble where those laws function that way but it will be small and only work in isolation as in the face of the greater collective of Sleepers, will bow to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203050#post1203050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why for the longest time, I have considered magic and science to be different from each other. Science tries to apply rules and deductive reasoning to how things work. Magic chooses to ignore those laws and reasoning, making it beyond the realm of scientific explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, that's against Mage: the Ascension. Magic, Faith, Science, they're all one and the same. They are how mere mortals can comprehend the Reality-altering powers at their fingertips and are ultimately an incomplete understanding because to fully and truly understand it is to become... well God basically. To cease to be something mortals can comprehend and become something beyond.<br /> <br /> In Mage: the Ascension, everybody is right, everybody is wrong because none of them can have truly complete picture of everything.<br /> <br /> In fact, that's actually built into the gameplay. As a Mage gains more understanding, they start discarding Foci because they are beginning to realize that they don't need their Foci, that their Beliefs are flawed and incomplete.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203050#post1203050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they want an even playing field, then the Technocracy could easily settle for using pocket dimensions, and give everybody (or at least every mage) the freedom to create their own personalized universes. That way, everyone is happy without stepping on anybody's toes.<br /> <br /> <br /> But no, they don't trust us to wield that kind of power. And if they don't trust us, then why in the hell would we trust them? Because they claim to have the vision necessary to lead us into the future? Yeah, just how many tyrannical dictators have used that exact line of reasoning to justify their own regimes? And how often did such regimes end in disaster as a result of their leader's hubris?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that won't work. As I said, for the Sleepers they affect the Consensus through their subconscious which includes their doubts and hesitations. One of the biggest problems any Mage group has in spreading their beliefs is that even if the Sleepers buy into it, many will privately or even subconsciously doubt it. The thought we've all had, 'It's too good to be true'. And that's all it takes for it to come apart or worse, cause Paradox for the poor Sleepers. In fact, that's why modern medical procedures and drugs don't always were or cause side effects, the Sleepers think it's too good to be true and the Consensus makes it so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T11:31:31-07:00","id":1203075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203050#post1203050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, yes, I can.<br /> <br /> 1 - I was raised in a religious household, though eventually renounced.<br /> <br /> 2 - I have always been fascinated by mythology and the occult<br /> <br /> 3 - I was a <b>true believer</b> in magic and the supernatural when I was younger.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as for the only source of power being the directly linked to the strength of your mind: That is exactly what I think of when it comes to using magic. I've often heard the story that magic operates in accordance with ancient laws and how there are some things that it can't accomplish.<br /> <br /> <br /> I reject this idea entirely. If magic is the power to warp reality (which it seems to be in Mage), and it is governed by the strength of your imagination, then that would logically mean that magic has no limitations. As long as you believe in it, it becomes possible, regardless of the general consensus is to the contrary. In laymen's terms, you dictate the rules, which are as malleable as your own interpretation of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's why for the longest time, I have considered magic and science to be different from each other. Science tries to apply rules and deductive reasoning to how things work. Magic chooses to ignore those laws and reasoning, making it beyond the realm of scientific explanation.<br /> <br /> <br /> If they want an even playing field, then the Technocracy could easily settle for using pocket dimensions, and give everybody (or at least every mage) the freedom to create their own personalized universes. That way, everyone is happy without stepping on anybody's toes.<br /> <br /> <br /> But no, they don't trust us to wield that kind of power. And if they don't trust us, then why in the hell would we trust them? Because they claim to have the vision necessary to lead us into the future? Yeah, just how many tyrannical dictators have used that exact line of reasoning to justify their own regimes? And how often did such regimes end in disaster as a result of their leader's hubris?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This has never been a discussion about <i>why </i>magic(k) works. It's about whether or not it <i>should.</i><br /> <br /> Not to come across as condescending, but I don't think you fully comprehend the scope of how horrifying a world where local belief determines reality would be.<br /> <br /> The grim truth is that yes, the Union has written unicorns and rune casting and giant mechs out of the consensus. But do you know what else they wrote out of the consensus? Among other things:<ul><li>Divinely enforced caste systems</li> <li>&quot;race realism&quot; (I hesitate to call it &quot;scientific racism&quot; because it's about the farthest thing from science you can get)</li> <li>Human sacrifice being necessary to continue on with everyday life</li> <li>Every culture having their own divine patron, each telling them that they have the inborn right to take over the world.</li> </ul>I personally can't even comprehend the horror that would be that world. A world where worldwide conflict never ceases and exists on a scale we couldn't even dream of, because Amatarasu or Wotan or Quetzalcoatl or YHWH can just waltz through the Gauntlet and not only tell their chosen people that they're <i>right </i>for wanting to exterminate all other cultures, but giving them the tools to do it.<br /> <br /> We have the freedom to choose what we believe in this world because, if we choose something awful, worst case scenario, we murder some people. In the WoD, if you choose to believe in something awful, you could easily bring about Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> In a world where belief can literally snuff out the sun or wipe an entire eon from history, the debate about freedom of faith is no longer about human rights or civil liberties.<br /> <br /> It's the gun control argument on a cosmic scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 04-04-2018, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T11:41:59-07:00","id":1203080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203057#post1203057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I suspect that when <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> finally gets published, we'll see a much more multi-cultural Technocracy. We already know from its description that it will cover the Asian and African Technocracies as well as the conventional Technocracy; and I suspect that the upcoming reorganization hinted at in M20 will end up replacing the five Eurocentric Conventions with a set of Conventions drawing from at least three culturally diverse sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly...I hope not. I really, <b><i>really</i></b> hope not. WW/OPP doesn't exactly have the best track record for creating cultural-specific fatsplats, and while it's true they're getting <i>better</i>, they're not quite there in my mind when it comes to justifying something like this. One of the more teeth-grating MtAs books I'd read was <i>Dragons of the East</i>, particularly the eastern Technocracy and how they tried to jackknife Kindred of the East content in there. Given what's come already, I'd expect:<br /> <br /> 1. A focus on what they call themselves and their Methodologies.<br /> 2. A treatise on why they hate the European Technocracy. Which will invariably have something to do with, for some reason, their culture's mystics.<br /> 3. A treatise on how they plan to fuck over the European Technocracy, and <i>somehow</i> win. Which will invariably have something to do with allying with their culture's mystics.<br /> 4. A list of culture-centric Procedures and Devices, because we gotta have some crunch to sell books.<br /> 5. Merits and flaws that invoke cultural stereo--...I mean, <i>arche</i>-types, and local/cultural myths and beliefs.<br /> <br /> I'd actually rather just see a detailed, comprehensive, treatise on how the Technocracy originally infiltrated the areas when they were still the Order of Reason, exported their beliefs and methods, and adapted that of the locals' to align more closely with Reason, and the challenges and pitfalls of keeping the Technocracy together in a post-Cold War, post-colonial, and eventually globalist, world. Stuff like,<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Mao...<b>ugh</b>. This is why Utopianism never works, and why utopianists need to be drug out into the street and shot. But you didn't hear that from me, last thing I need is some black suit pencil-neck sniffing around my offshore accounts trying to fabricate a case to un-person me, I don't want the kind of bureaucratic headache it is to make sure his pet projects get defunded, and no financial backer would touch him with a ten-meter pole again.<br /> <br /> That bastard Mao finally croaking was Christmas, Kwanzaa, Chanukah, Boxing Day, all our birthdays, Valentine's, and that one day you get your friend or SO something nice just to be a good person, all rolled into one. The biggest, most populated, country on Earth, with resources of value and rarity to put the sea of light, sweet crude in the Gulf to shame. A nation with a legalist tradition that goes back to before the days when the Romans were crucifying hippies. A backwards, isolated, totalitarian state nobody <b>really</b> cared about, with a sudden power vacuum to be filled...by us. Because we were <b>always</b> here, we were just waiting for our moment.<br /> <br /> And it's here. Forget NYC. Forget Chicago. London decided to immolate itself, and Zurich and Berlin are well on their way. Those idiots in Dubai want to carry the torch, but they're bankrupting themselves kowtowing to a global economic regime that's already dead and doesn't know it. Moscow? Moscow's playing the fool, acting like they're trying to be a quaint also-ran that can't punch in the &quot;big boys and girls&quot; weight class, but they've been in on the joke for nearly thirty years, ever since the Chicago and Washington boys tried clipping their wings when the Iron Curtain fell. They're already coming here to Beijing, and in ten years' time this will be where they <b>only</b> come.<br /> <br /> We lead the world in renewables development. We lead the world in space exploration -- and contracts and ties to the Void Engineers. Automation? Iteration-X loves us. In ten years' time we'll be making the West look like they're still using leeches in terms of pharmaceuticals, medicine, and bio-tech research, which makes us blue-chip investments in the Progenitors' eyes.<br /> <br /> The 'New World Order&quot;? look around you. Look at the society which you're visiting.We do what they do, more efficiently, and with a lower bottom line, simply by appealing to people's basic human desire to belong to something greater than themselves, and ensuring being a part of something greater than themselves is the most lucrative and rational thing to do. Let the NWO and the Western Syndicate talk about a Technocratic Cold War, Civil War, or whatever -- it's over and it hasn't even started. We won.&quot;</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T11:48:43-07:00","id":1203082,"title":"","content":"All that assumes that the WOD is fully metaphysically idealistic, which the books themselves are very contradictory about. Some parts will imply a metaphysically idealistic world, where the world was flat until humanity collectively decided it was round, and others imply a world that would be mostly scientific even if the technocrats had never existed, with the fight being over things in the margins.<br /> <br /> It's a plot-hole in the premise of Mage, really, since a fully metaphysically idealistic world would have a wildly different history. It is highly unlikely that technocrats would even come into being in such a world, since humans are lazy and would much rather believe that just a quick prayer to the spirits fixes everything. Humans would have decided on something very different very early and that something would have stuck, preventing the technocrats from ever coming into being.<br /> <br /> Yet, if we take the premise that the technocratic view is mostly correct, and the fight is really over things in the margins, then the Traditions really just become a bunch of terrorists threatening to let monsters into the world over trivia like aesthetic preferences.<br /> <br /> The books take it as a given that neither of those things are true, which is a huge plothole. Especially since it goes back and forth on implying that one or the other is true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T11:50:07-07:00","id":1203084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203066#post1203066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That will be kind of difficult to imagine. Technology is technology, I don't think it adheres to any specific form of nationality. It's basically just bragging rights over which culture was responsible for inventing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> But this debate is getting out of hand. The original post wasn't a discussing on why the Technocracy did what they did. It was more about pointing out the consequences for what they did and how it impacts humanity's future going forward. Sure, to an awakened mind, the distance between Earth and that planet made out of diamond is only about 60 feet beyond Mars. But the rest of humanity believes the distance is significantly greater. It also believes that traveling that distance in a manner that is even remotely convenient is scientifically impossible.<br /> <br /> <br /> This isn't something as simple as designing the first airplane. We knew that flight was possible, we've seen many different species of animals capable of achieving flight and we modeled the airplane off their design. We have never seen anything travel faster than the speed of light, nor seen a living being frozen in ice for thousands of years and manage to survive after being thawed out. No, this kind of technology is a violation of the laws of physics and biology alike. And if the Technocracy wants us to surpass those limitations, then they're going to have to demonstrate that doing so is possible, and explain it in such a way that we can comprehend beyond equating it to the stuff of miracles.</div> </div> </div> </div>If, by \u201cthe rest of humanity\u201d, you mean \u201cthe scientific community\u201d, I'll accept your point. However, the scientific community is not the last word on the Consensus, as much as the Technocracy has been pushing it to be. And I'm not talking about mysticism, either: Cinematic License (p.616) and hypernarrative are examples of things the Consensus accepts that are not scientifically sound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:01:28-07:00","id":1203087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203070#post1203070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that's not how it is in Mage: the Ascension. There are concrete laws of Reality created by the Consensus. That's why Reality works as it does. Magic, Enlightened Science, Willworking, whatever you wish to call it, is the bending or breaking of those laws to achieve something. And only the Awakened can truly do individually. For the Sleepers it is simply their collective subconscious will working together to establish the laws of the Consensus.<br /> <br /> Sure, you can get groups of Sleepers to agree on things contrary to those laws and create a bubble where those laws function that way but it will be small and only work in isolation as in the face of the greater collective of Sleepers, will bow to it.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But the very idea of consensus means that that is, in fact, how things work. Those laws of reality exist because we believe they exist. If we stop believing they exist, then the laws of reality will stop existing, or be replaced with whatever consensus decides to go with from that point on.<br /> <br /> The way I rationalize the Sleeper Consensus is the same principle as performing a cooperative ritual or spell. They're combining their magic to achieve an agreed upon outcome. So when an Awakened mage tries to cast magic, it can be described as a counter spell of some kind. The Mage using their willpower to cancel out that of the Sleepers. But since there's only 1 Mage and like 50 Sleepers present at the time of the casting, the effects of the counter spell don't last very long.<br /> <br /> <br /> If this were Mage the Awakening, I'd personally side with the Silver Ladder. Not because they want humanity to dominate the universe, but because of their philosophy that everybody has an inherent right to the power of magic, and their long term goal of casting down the Exarchs, who seem like a more sinister version of the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:04:58-07:00","id":1203091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">But this debate is getting out of hand. The original post wasn't a discussing on why the Technocracy did what they did. It was more about pointing out the consequences for what they did and how it impacts humanity's future going forward. Sure, to an awakened mind, the distance between Earth and that planet made out of diamond is only about 60 feet beyond Mars. But the rest of humanity believes the distance is significantly greater. It also believes that traveling that distance in a manner that is even remotely convenient is scientifically impossible.<br /> <br /> <br /> This isn't something as simple as designing the first airplane. We knew that flight was possible, we've seen many different species of animals capable of achieving flight and we modeled the airplane off their design. We have never seen anything travel faster than the speed of light, nor seen a living being frozen in ice for thousands of years and manage to survive after being thawed out. No, this kind of technology is a violation of the laws of physics and biology alike. And if the Technocracy wants us to surpass those limitations, then they're going to have to demonstrate that doing so is possible, and explain it in such a way that we can comprehend beyond equating it to the stuff of miracles.</span></span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Even right now, there is serious and professional scientific research about how to achieve space travel beyond the speed of light, and no scientist it's proclaiming heresy merely because doing so it's impossible <i>with the resources we have right now</i>.<br /> <br /> I repeat, lasers were an impossibility just 70 years ago (Einstein himself said that lasers would be too hard to create). Laws of physics and even of mathematics were &quot;violated&quot; several times in modern history (altrough a scientific mind would preffer to talk about a &quot;change in Paradigm&quot; or something like that), that's how science works. Sorry, but the idea that &quot;science has hit a wall with this issue and we will all die because of that (in billons of years)&quot; it's plainly ludicrous to me, it doesn't follow from how the actual scientific development works, it doesnt follow from human history.<br /> <br /> And if current science can change Paradigm now and then, the Technocracy can change the rules whenever they want with all the more reason. Worst case scenario they will end creating another batch of Etherites.<br /> <br /> The idea that the power that science gave to use could end causing the end of the world (like, say, from nuclear warfare) it's more realist. It holds more water in my opinion, among other things because we don't need to wait billons of years to get to that point, we already have the resources to do so.<br /> <br /> If such a thing were to happen in WoD, the Technocracy has the resources (mundane and supernatural) to predict such event and prevent it. Still, the OoH does lament that &quot;humanity has been given the power of our gods&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-04-2018, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:17:59-07:00","id":1203095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203087#post1203087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the very idea of consensus means that that is, in fact, how things work. Those laws of reality exist because we believe they exist. If we stop believing they exist, then the laws of reality will stop existing, or be replaced with whatever consensus decides to go with from that point on.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus\">I have a whole article about this.</a> The takeaway is that the Consensus does not, in fact, create the laws of reality; it only influences them. And it doesn't do so by a simple majority vote, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:22:33-07:00","id":1203098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203091#post1203091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">steemed <br /> <br /> Even right now, there is serious and professional scientific research about how to achieve space travel beyond the speed of light, and no scientist it's proclaiming heresy merely because doing so it's impossible <i>with the resources we have right now</i>. <br /> <br /> I repeat, lasers were an impossibility just 70 years ago (Einstein himself said that lasers would be too hard to create). Laws of physics and even of mathematics were &amp;quot;violated&amp;quot; several times in modern history (altrough a scientific mind would preffer to talk about a &amp;quot;change in Paradigm&amp;quot; or something like that), that's how science works. Sorry, but the idea that &amp;quot;science has hit a wall with this issue and we will all die because of that (in billons of years)&amp;quot; it's plainly ludicrous to me, it doesn't follow from how the actual scientific development works, it doesnt follow from human history.<br /> <br /> And if current science can change Paradigm now and then, the Technocracy can change the rules whenever they want with all the more reason. Worst case scenario they will end creating another batch of Etherites. <br /> <br /> The idea that the power that science gave to use could end causing the end of the world (like, say, from nuclear warfare) it's more realist. It holds more water in my opinion, among other things because we don't need to wait billons of years to get to that point, we already have the resources to do so. <br /> <br /> If such a thing were to happen in WoD, the Technocracy has the resources (mundane and supernatural) to predict such event and prevent it. Still, the OoH does lament that &amp;quot;humanity has been given the power of our gods&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And even if Aleph is wrong, and that in the real world FTL truly is impossible, mindsets like his would be a significant part of the Consensus in <b>Mage</b> \u2014 meaning that FTL isn't necessarily impossible in its cosmology even if it's impossible in the real world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:25:37-07:00","id":1203099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203080#post1203080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly...I hope not. I really, <b><i>really</i></b> hope not. WW/OPP doesn't exactly have the best track record for creating cultural-specific fatsplats, and while it's true they're getting <i>better</i>, they're not quite there in my mind when it comes to justifying something like this. One of the more teeth-grating MtAs books I'd read was <i>Dragons of the East</i>, particularly the eastern Technocracy and how they tried to jackknife Kindred of the East content in there. Given what's come already, I'd expect:<br /> <br /> 1. A focus on what they call themselves and their Methodologies.<br /> 2. A treatise on why they hate the European Technocracy. Which will invariably have something to do with, for some reason, their culture's mystics.<br /> 3. A treatise on how they plan to fuck over the European Technocracy, and <i>somehow</i> win. Which will invariably have something to do with allying with their culture's mystics.<br /> 4. A list of culture-centric Procedures and Devices, because we gotta have some crunch to sell books.<br /> 5. Merits and flaws that invoke cultural stereo--...I mean, <i>arche</i>-types, and local/cultural myths and beliefs.<br /> <br /> I'd actually rather just see a detailed, comprehensive, treatise on how the Technocracy originally infiltrated the areas when they were still the Order of Reason, exported their beliefs and methods, and adapted that of the locals' to align more closely with Reason, and the challenges and pitfalls of keeping the Technocracy together in a post-Cold War, post-colonial, and eventually globalist, world.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I agree.<br /> <br /> Albeit I would think that an exploration of the antecesors of the Technocracy in human history could and should include more than the Order of Reason. The story of the many groups of technomages and mages devoted to hunting monsters or to the ideal of control that were willing to join the OoR when it started to expand itself trough the world could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:30:46-07:00","id":1203101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203082#post1203082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that assumes that the WOD is fully metaphysically idealistic, which the books themselves are very contradictory about. Some parts will imply a metaphysically idealistic world, where the world was flat until humanity collectively decided it was round, and others imply a world that would be mostly scientific even if the technocrats had never existed, with the fight being over things in the margins.<br /> <br /> It's a plot-hole in the premise of Mage, really, since a fully metaphysically idealistic world would have a wildly different history. It is highly unlikely that technocrats would even come into being in such a world, since humans are lazy and would much rather believe that just a quick prayer to the spirits fixes everything. Humans would have decided on something very different very early and that something would have stuck, preventing the technocrats from ever coming into being.<br /> <br /> Yet, if we take the premise that the technocratic view is mostly correct, and the fight is really over things in the margins, then the Traditions really just become a bunch of terrorists threatening to let monsters into the world over trivia like aesthetic preferences.<br /> <br /> The books take it as a given that neither of those things are true, which is a huge plothole. Especially since it goes back and forth on implying that one or the other is true.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a plot hole; it's freedom to run the game how you want to. Especially in M20, I take the position that the Traditions and the Technocracy each have their own unifying philosophies, and that both have evidence to back up their claims: the truth is probably more of a \u201cblind men and the elephant\u201d thing, with each side having latched onto an aspect of the truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:41:55-07:00","id":1203106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203099#post1203099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, I agree.<br /> <br /> Albeit I would think that an exploration of the antecesors of the Technocracy in human history could and should include more than the Order of Reason. The story of the many groups of technomages and mages devoted to hunting monsters or to the ideal of control that were willing to join the OoR when it started to expand itself trough the world could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I think would be more interesting would be if the many groups of technomages and mages devoted to hunting monsters or to the ideal of <s>control</s>reason weren't necessarily willing to join the Order of Reason when it started expanding through the world, but often <i>were</i> willing to ally with them \u2014 and only now, these alliances are being forged into a single Union that owes as much to ancient China as to Victorian England.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T13:13:55-07:00","id":1203111,"title":"","content":"The thing is, the Order was founded by Enlightened minds from Europe, the Middle East and Asia. And while the Cabal of Pure Thought did scare off some of the Muslims and I would assume other non-Christians, others stayed. So the Order should already have a foothold there unless they decide to retcon things again.<br /> <br /> Well unless Dragons of the East retconned that. I don't know as I haven't read that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T14:05:06-07:00","id":1203128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203099#post1203099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Albeit I would think that an exploration of the antecesors of the Technocracy in human history could and should include more than the Order of Reason. The story of the many groups of technomages and mages devoted to hunting monsters or to the ideal of control that were willing to join the OoR when it started to expand itself trough the world could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't necessarily need to be a one-way street.<br /> <br /> Case in point, when I ran my old MtAs game fifteen years ago, one of the PC's was a Japanese Etherite, and his father was a Technocrat. One story in particular involved the PC's going to Japan, to hunt a Nephandus who they'd been after for some time, and they ended up working with the Technocracy to do it through said PC's connections. Which meant I ended up having to do my background reading on the Technocracy in Asia...throwing it all out because it was more or less garbage, and writing my own history.<br /> <br /> Long story short, the real history of the collapse of the Tokugawa era was that the Tokugawa government was hopelessly indebted to the merchant caste, who was the lowest-status caste in Japanese feudal society. The samurai caste got around this by forgiving their own debts, and continuing to extort money from the merchants. Needless to say, the merchants didn't like this. So, when the Sat-Cho Alliance rose up against the Tokugawa government in the 1860's, the merchants backed them and the rest was history.<br /> <br /> For my Mage game, I'd decided the mystics had backed the priesthood and samurai all this time. A foundation for the Order of Reason had already been built up among the merchant and artisan caste, led by Mitsui- and Sumitomo-affiliated mages who resented Tokugawa and mystic rule. During the Meiji Restoration and numerous samurai rebellions, this Japanese proto-OoR found itself at the top of the newly-forming pecking order, and Mitsui and Sumitomo were joined by Mitsubishi and Yasuda. When the Japanese government started really sending out citizens to study at Western universities and companies to learn and return with their knowledge, Zaibatsu-affiliated Mages went out too, to learn under the nascent Technocratic Union.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy was entirely happy with this, because it was their non-imperialist inroad to Japan. So were the Japanese mages, since their regime was to Westernize, become economically and militarily powerful, and grow their sphere of interest to prevent further Western influence or control. During this time, the Zaibatsu were entirely independent from the Technocratic Union, but close enough to the Technocracy's own ideology and goals, and not European enough, to be worth assimilation or further attention.<br /> <br /> Except, the Zaibatsu fucked up big time. The majority of their people, already being merchants and interested in business and economics, went to study under Exchequers. Of the minority, most of those went to study under the Electrodyne Engineers. A handful of others went to study elsewhere. When the Etherites abandoned the Technocratic Union, the Japanese Etherites largely remained because they were loyal to zaibatsu and country, not Convention; this drew (entirely warranted) questions from the Ivory Tower about the zaibatsus' true loyalties. driving a rift between the Zaibatsu and the larger Technocracy. But by then, Japan was almost entirely of, by, and for the Syndicate, albeit a <i>ludicrously</i> militarized and nationalist version of the Syndicate, wherein the Zaibatsu acted as miniature Conventions within the larger whole.<br /> <br /> After WWII, the Technocracy stepped in, busted up the Zaibatsu, demilitarized the Japanese Syndicate along with the rest of the country, and split up/re-educated the Japanese mages to align to the contemporary Conventions and Methodologies. Of course, the Japanese Syndicate was too powerful and entrenched, and the measures taken too little, so the Japanese Syndicate reformed as the keiretsu, but this time around with <i>just enough</i> external oversight by other Conventions to stay under the radar.<br /> <br /> So, basically, what I'd written was an example of a non-European collective of mages observing the Technocratic Union, learning and taking from them what would work respective to their own culture and societal goals, and creating their own vaguely Technocratic society of mages which stayed independent from the greater whole for nearly a century. And, when the Technocracy eventually intervened, they adapted enough to make the Technocracy happy, while maintaining enough independence to maintain their own group identity and pursue their own goals in alignment with the greater Technocratic vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 04-04-2018, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T10:18:33-07:00","id":1203448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203028#post1203028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Objectively, in M20? No.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times New Roman\">Unlike previous editions of <b>Mage</b> (aside from <b>Sorcerers Crusade</b>), <b>Mage 20</b> does not default to a Traditions-centric viewpoint. Instead, we're presenting a wide range of potential <b>Mage</b> characters. With that range comes a bigger perspective on the Awakened experience, so the following chapter features as objective a view as you could possibly get from a world in which reality is anything but certain.</span><br /> \u2014 page 120</div>The chapter in question covers Awakened history and the various factions of the Ascension War. But the even-handed approach isn't confined to that chapter: throughout the book, you have statements like \u201cmystic mages blame the Technocracy, the Technocrats blame the mystics, and both sides of that divide are right.\u201d (p.75)<br /> <br /> See also the Common Ground section on pp.349\u2013353, which includes several examples of how a troupe including both Technocrats and non-Technocrats can be brought together and given enough rationale to stay together to hold a chronicle together. Chapter Seven ends with summaries of five types of Chronicles: the Traditions, the Technocracy, the Disparates, the Orphans, and the Mixed-Faction.<br /> <br /> The closest M20 comes to an anti-Technocrat bias is the way it occasionally presents Technocratic terminology off to the side, and tends to use the Traditions' terminology by default. But that's more a case of practicality than bias.<br /> <br /> You're free to choose to see the Technocracy as the bad guys; but that's <i>your choice,</i> not something M20 pushes on you. You might even decide that the Technocracy is objectively bad, and that anyone who sees them as the good guys is delusional. M20 actively warns <i>against</i> such certainty, citing it as a symptom of hubris while indicating that it's an all-too-common flaw among mages of all stripes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We must be reading two profoundly different books, between the overt Orwellian bits to the plethora of heroic factions within the Technocracy working around the system because its broken to the Default explanation for the Disparate Alliance, I would say the default assumption is that the Technocracy is the Antagonist Faction... even in Technocracy chronicles.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T11:17:57-07:00","id":1203461,"title":"","content":"Eh, a lot of Tradition stories also take it as a given that the top tradition brass are hidebound and corrupt. It's a common trope in all adventure fiction that the hero is the rebel who sees clearly the problems the top guys have become too lazy, corrupt, complacent, whatever to see. This is true even when the story takes the view that the faction as a whole is the good guy or at least the lighter shade of grey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T12:46:22-07:00","id":1203489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203448#post1203448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We must be reading two profoundly different books, between the overt Orwellian bits to the plethora of heroic factions within the Technocracy working around the system because its broken to the Default explanation for the Disparate Alliance, I would say the default assumption is that the Technocracy is the Antagonist Faction... even in Technocracy chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's definitely plenty of support for playing the Technocracy as antagonists if that's what you want to do; I've never said otherwise. What I'm taking issue with is the claim that M20 presents using the Technocracy as the antagonists as the <i>default</i> option. It explicitly does not. <br /> <br /> No, the default antagonist faction in M20 is the Nephandi \u2014 even to the extent that much of what's wrong with the Technocracy and the Traditions is blamed on them. <br /> <br /> The default explanation for the Disparate Alliance that you alluded to isn't \u201cThe Technocracy is a threat\u201d; it's \u201cthe Nephandi have infiltrated the Technocracy\u201d. It's their shared belief that the Nephandi are puppetmasters who must be stopped at all costs that's bringing them together \u2014 and it's their suspicion that the Nephandi may have infiltrated the Traditions too that keeps them from approaching the Council with their concerns. <br /> <br /> The heroic factions within the Technocracy that are working around the system are there for Storytellers who want to tell stories along the lines of \u201cthe Technocracy is corrupt but redeemable\u201d. It doesn't mean that they're the default approach for a Technocracy Chronicle; indeed, the section in Chapter Seven about a Technocracy Chronicle, while it does say that intrigue is featured in nearly all Technocratic Chronicles, doesn't even mention the dissident factions until the final paragraph, and then only to note that they're an exception to the way other Technocracy Chronicles work. So no, the Technocracy is <i>not</i> the default antagonist of a Technocratic Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T14:15:30-07:00","id":1203519,"title":"","content":"One thing to remember about a Technocracy chronicle is, you are playing the winners. So even if the Technocracy is the lighter shade of grey, you as a technocrat are not the underdog. At best, you're the rich guy drone-striking evilish poor people with rusty junk weapons. Which inherently limits the drama of playing Techno vs Traddie from the Techno perspective.<br /> <br /> So a Technocracy chronicle is going to be more often about being the winner who doesn't want his victory to fall apart from internal corruption.<br /> <br /> That's not to say it's impossible to run a Techno chronicle where you are locally the underdog, or for that matter, nor is it impossible to run a Tradition chronicle focusing on internal corruption. But the tendency is going to be stronger towards running Techno chronicles as fights against internal corruption, and Tradition chronicles as guerilla stuff. Being the winner and loser respectively just lends itself to those results with less contrived plot-points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T17:35:30-07:00","id":1203590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203519#post1203519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to remember about a Technocracy chronicle is, you are playing the winners. So even if the Technocracy is the lighter shade of grey, you as a technocrat are not the underdog. At best, you're the rich guy drone-striking evilish poor people with rusty junk weapons. Which inherently limits the drama of playing Techno vs Traddie from the Techno perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Playing James Bond or CSI or NCIS or Criminal Minds has inherently limited drama. [/sarcasm]<br /> <br /> And that's just NWO. You could also join the Space Marines and fight threats against your home on <i>their</i> turf in order to ensure they never get near <i>your</i> turf. Movies like Saving Private Ryan could be used as inspiration for such VE stories. And there <i>are</i> still a few Void Engineers exploring strange new worlds, if you don't want to go the military route. For the Progenitors, you could do a sci-fi spin on medical dramas. And so on. Anyone who thinks that you have to be the underdog to have sufficient drama to carry a chronicle simply isn't using enough imagination \u2014 and it really doesn't take much imagination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T18:11:35-07:00","id":1203602,"title":"","content":"Well modern James Bond movies are exactly what I'm talking about. Bond doesn't really fight terrorists, except as minor cold-open villains. He fights corrupt establishment figures. Modern Spectre isn't some organization of third world terrorists. It's an organization of what in Mage would be Syndicate and NWO types corrupting the establishment from within. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spectre_(2015_film\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spectre_(2015_film</a>) The gist of modern spy movies is that the &quot;good&quot; guys won, and are now rotting from the inside. Hell, it's even become part of superhero movies, where SHIELD has secretly been massively infiltrated by Hydra, and even the non-Hydra leaders will nuke New York if things get hectic. Or Homeland, where the biggest evil of all is the new President.<br /> <br /> For that matter, the quintessential Space Marine movie, &quot;Aliens&quot;, has the aliens mainly be a threat because the corporation is so obsessed with controlling a new resource that they sabotage the survival of their own troops. And &quot;Starship Troopers&quot; has the subtext of being a propaganda movie created by a government that destroyed one of its own cities to justify a war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-05-2018, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T18:38:34-07:00","id":1203608,"title":"","content":"Yeah; there are modern films in the espionage and war genres that paint your bosses as the bad guys. And <i>if you want to play the Technocracy that way, you can.</i> But you don't <i>have</i> to: there's plenty of drama to be had <i>without</i> assuming that your bosses are corrupt. If that means going to older sources of inspiration, so be it; for what it's worth, modern Hollywood isn't really my scene. <br /> <br /> Though you might do just as well going to TV or novels: note that other than James Bond, my NWO examples came from TV. And the Jason Bourne <i>books</i> are <i>very</i> different from the movies after the first one: in fact, the first book ends with Jason rejoining the CIA; and the sequels deal with the CIA going after various terrorist threats. And don't get me started on the Starship Troopers movie: that thing was a total betrayal of the book it was based on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-05-2018, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:51:31-07:00","id":1203643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203023#post1203023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it's like playing an adventurer that wants to get rid of all the dragons and undead and evil wizards that threaten his hometown. Y'know. Like an adventurer. The Technocracy doesn't want to get rid of imagination and wonder, they want to harness it in a way that allows it to do as little damage as possible.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In other words, ridding the world of everything a quest giver would want to hire you for. Or do you expect the adventure to offer his services performing mundane labor and household chores once there's no epic quest to go on?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If I wanted a world without magic and superstition, <i>I wouldn't be playing a friggin mage</i>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So yeah, I'm going to go with the idea of the Technocracy being the default antagonists because of their aversion to what being a mage is all about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, did a little bit of research into the setting. Sounds like me and the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1bBYL73aubg\" target=\"_blank\">Marauders</a> and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X2mYMmLpe_M\" target=\"_blank\">Nephandi</a> have a few similar ideas in regards to the use of magic. Absolute freedom, unbound by the laws of God or Man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-05-2018, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:24:35-07:00","id":1203662,"title":"","content":"Similar to who: the Traditions? Because one thing the Technocracy is <i>not</i> about is absolute freedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-05-2018, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:28:01-07:00","id":1203666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203662#post1203662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar to who: the Traditions? Because one thing the Technocracy is <i>not</i> about is absolute freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, did the links not show up properly? I'm pretty sure I said Marauders and Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-05-2018, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:29:24-07:00","id":1203668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203643#post1203643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In other words, ridding the world of everything a quest giver would want to hire you for.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is literally the opposite of what @Nilbog said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:30:17-07:00","id":1203669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203666#post1203666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait, did the links not show up properly? I'm pretty sure I said <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1bBYL73aubg&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Marauders</a> and <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X2mYMmLpe_M&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Nephandi</a></div> </div> </div> </div> You did. Who are you comparing them to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:33:24-07:00","id":1203672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203668#post1203668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is literally the opposite of what @Nilbog said.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My post that they were replying to was comparing the Technocracy to being adventurers who want to rid the world of quest givers. I.e, they're mages who want to remove belief in the supernatural and therefor remove the very idea of being a mage in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:37:11-07:00","id":1203673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203669#post1203669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You did. Who are you comparing them to?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm comparing them to my own views on the use of magic, or a world in which the supernatural is real.<br /> <br /> As I said before, I find it easier playing controversial (i.e villain) type characters than some other players might be comfortable with.<br /> <br /> Being a Willworker who doesn't give a shit about Consensus / Paradox and does whatever they please sounds appealing to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-05-2018, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:39:44-07:00","id":1203674,"title":"","content":"And Nilbog's point was that it's a false comparison: the Technocracy is <i>not</i> trying to get rid of quest givers; it's trying to resolve the quests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:45:03-07:00","id":1203676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203673#post1203673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm comparing them to my own views on the use of magic, or a world in which the supernatural is real.<br /> <br /> As I said before, I find it easier playing controversial (i.e villain) type characters than some other players might be comfortable with.<br /> <br /> Being a Willworker who doesn't give a shit about Consensus / Paradox and does whatever they please sounds appealing to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the Marauders, then. Have fun, if you can find a Storyteller willing to let you play one. <br /> <br /> That's not the Nephandi, though: they're not about absolute freedom; they're about nihilism. They don't have the ability to override everyone else's reality with their own; that's something unique to Marauders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:56:06-07:00","id":1203684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203676#post1203676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not the Nephandi, though: they're not about absolute freedom; they're about nihilism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. I don't remember which topic it was, but we recently had one discussing how Nihilists simply wouldn't have any faith or motivation to do much of anything because they see the universe as ultimately being pointless.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nephandi see the universe as being pointless, but unlike those who subscribe to nihilism, they believe that it doesn't have to be. They want to destroy the universe and replace it with something they genuinely believe is better than what we have now. In that regard, they're a lot like revolutionaries, even if they do subscribe to allegedly darker powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:03:45-07:00","id":1203686,"title":"","content":"The Nephandi are not nihilists. Nihilists believe there is no such thing as objective meaning. That is to say, that &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; do not exist in the sense that the laws of thermodynamics exist. Nihilists do not want to destroy the universe. It's just that if they want to protect the universe or help people, they accept that their desire to protect the universe and/or help people is just a personal preference, neither &quot;good&quot; nor &quot;evil&quot;.Nephandi, conversely, DO believe in objective good and evil, and are on evil's side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:06:24-07:00","id":1203690,"title":"","content":"Essentially, a nihilist doesn't believe in anything, while the Nephandi believe in capital-n Nothing. It's a kind of esoteric difference, but it's there.<br /> <br /> Of all the factions in Mage, the Nephandi have the <i>least </i>free will. They aren't ingenious ubermenschen bucking the system and giving &quot;conventional morality&quot; the finger; they are, first and foremost, <i>slaves </i>to the ruinous powers they serve, kept in the chains that are their broken souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 04-06-2018, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:18:28-07:00","id":1203696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203690#post1203690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, a nihilist doesn't believe in anything, while the Nephandi believe in capital-n Nothing. It's a kind of esoteric difference, but it's there.<br /> <br /> Of all the factions in Mage, the Nephandi have the <i>least </i>free will. They aren't ingenious ubermenschen bucking the system and giving &quot;conventional morality&quot; the finger; they are, first and foremost, <i>slaves </i>to the ruinous powers they serve, kept in the chains that are their broken souls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not the description for them I've been lead to believe by several different accounts.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi believe that this particular version of reality is wrong, broken, corrupted and worthless. They want to see it destroyed so that a new reality can take its place. And they genuinely believe that this new version of reality will be an improvement over the previous one.<br /> <br /> You might consider them to be slaves to darker powers, but nobody forces you to become a Nephandi. The decision has to be made of your own free will, and the Nephandi made that choice, because they believed it was the right thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:31:40-07:00","id":1203702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203696#post1203696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's not the description for them I've been lead to believe by several different accounts.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi believe that this particular version of reality is wrong, broken, corrupted and worthless. They want to see it destroyed so that a new reality can take its place. And they genuinely believe that this new version of reality will be an improvement over the previous one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some say that, yes. But that's all window dressing. At the end of the day, the Nephandi are, to a one, broken, flailing husks of human beings desperately lashing out at a world they think owed them a better life than they had. They're stooges at best and nothing short of living sock puppets at worst, grotesque caricatures of powerful people caught at their lowest point and frozen in time at the nadir of their humanity.<br /> <br /> They may say that they think they're doing you a favor by freeing you from this rotten world, but at the end of the day, they don't think that because they don't really <i>think </i>at all. They act on anger and despair that has settled into contempt and hatred because, thanks to the parasite that is their broken Avatar, that's all they are anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203696#post1203696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might consider them to be slaves to darker powers, but nobody forces you to become a Nephandi. The decision has to be made of your own free will, and the Nephandi made that choice, because they believed it was the right thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the Widderslainte. And those physically forced into the Cauls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:42:12-07:00","id":1203706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203702#post1203702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Except for the Widderslainte. And those physically forced into the Cauls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Widderslainte are just people who already chose to become Nephandi in a previous life.<br /> <br /> <br /> I thought those physically forced into a Caul end up dying?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:59:34-07:00","id":1203710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203706#post1203706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Widderslainte are just people who already chose to become Nephandi in a previous life.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what is written in <i>the Book of Madness </i>2nd edition, a Widderslainte has an Avatar that belonged to a Nephandus, but she or he isn't this Nephandus reincarnated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T22:01:58-07:00","id":1203711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203706#post1203706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Widderslainte are just people who already chose to become Nephandi in a previous life.<br /> <br /> <br /> I thought those physically forced into a Caul end up dying?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring questions about the nature of identity and consciousness inherent in belief systems that center around reincarnation, there's an issue there: an Avatar isn't a part of the soul. They mix and match between incarnations. Nephandic Avatars are parasites that latch onto souls between lives. The previous incarnation of your soul didn't make that choice, the last soul attached to your Avatar did.<br /> <br /> But that misses the broader point here: The Nephandi are <i>miserable. </i>They don't go into the Caul because of some high-minded ideal of clearing away the refuse of the world. They do it because they're broken, miserable people that have been taken advantage of. The only urge the Nephandi feel more strongly than their hatred for their own painfully meaningless existence is the rage they feel at the world for allowing something like them to exist in the first place.Every Nephandus has a story about how the world betrayed and broke them, but that doesn't make them right. All they do is perpetuate the cycle of cruelty and hate.<br /> <br /> That's the tragedy of the Nephandic condition. You don't &quot;choose&quot; to be a Nephandus any more than you &quot;choose&quot; to become a junkie or a prostitute or to stay in an abusive relationship.<br /> <br /> The difference is, no matter how much they struggle, a Nephandus will never get better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T23:10:11-07:00","id":1203730,"title":"","content":"The Nephandi of M20 are not the Nephandi of the earlier editions. Brucato remade them for M20 to reflect a rather traumatic episode in his life that occurred sometime after he left Mage: a girl he knew befriended him and through that friendship very nearly tore his relationships apart. That's why M20 consistently focused on the \u201c<i>true</i> Nephandi\u201d being a distinctly <i>human</i> evil that operates by getting their enemies \u201cshooting at shadows\u2026 or at one another\u2026 while winning them over to your point of view, all the while seeming like their best friend in the world.\u201d (p.228)<br /> <br /> These new Nephandi are explicitly <i>not</i> \u201cslaves of the star-squid\u201d (pp.225\u2013226): \u201cThey don't serve Outer Gods, in truth. Nephandi simply recognize such beings as reflections of their own Enlightenment\u2026 a savage wisdom that see the Absolute in every living thing and knows what's waiting at the end of All.\u201d (p.226)<br /> <br /> And they're not interested in what comes next, if indeed they believe that there's <i>anything</i> that comes next: it's not \u201cburn everything down in order to let something new grow\u201d; it's \u201cburn everything down\u201d. If they can talk you into burning things down by hinting that it's a step toward a renewal, they're more than willing to do so; but that hint of a renewal is merely a ploy, not something they believe. No; the most sympathetic their actual view is is that they're performing a \u201cmercy killing\u201d: Reality is dying a slow, painful death, and there's no hope for a recovery; so they're trying to hurry it along. And even <i>that</i> argument might just be a ploy to lure you deeper into their philosophy.<br /> <br /> They're the true villains of the game; and Brucato changed them in M20 to reflect a true evil that he hadn't realized existed before he encountered it personally.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi of the earlier editions still exist; but they've been demoted to being \u201cstalking horses\u201d for M20's brand of Nephandi: they're the shadows mentioned in the above quote, the distractions the true Nephandi get you shooting at while they become your best friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-06-2018, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T23:46:05-07:00","id":1203736,"title":"","content":"Well, that's disappointing. Think I'll stick with the more positive outlook version, instead of the revamped one.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T00:39:58-07:00","id":1203744,"title":"","content":"That \u201cmore positive outlook version\u201d? That's never been the case in any edition of Mage. To the extent that such a view has ever been expressed by a Nephandus, it has always been a lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T01:29:55-07:00","id":1203754,"title":"","content":"For a long time, my interpretation of the Nephandi have been as people whose internal drives are geared towards the corrupt, cruel, destructive, and profane. It's not a matter of Reason - there's nothing reasonable about the Nephandi's goals, though they spin a lot of Logic about them that can entice or fool other people. Rather, their philosophical arguments exist to justify - to themselves more than anyone - what they feel in their hearts.<br /> <br /> What they feel, of course, being hate, loathing, bitterness, and sadism. While any normal person can learn to gain joy from cruelty or satisfaction from annihilation, for the Nephandi these are their ONLY pleasures. It's an emotional problem more than anything, and it's a problem packaged into their spiritually damaged Avatar. Their only positive reinforcement - their only spiritual fulfillment - arises from being the greatest bastards they can be. Every other aspect of Nephandic philosophy is built around rationalizing this in the Nephandus's mind, and secondarily towards giving a framework to be fed to other people in the effort of conversion.<br /> <br /> Under this framework, it's not impossible for a Widderslainte to be &quot;redeemed&quot;, at least in theory. It's just that being genuinely good comes neither naturally nor easily to a person born with an inverted Avatar. Nephandi, like normal people, have a free will that is complicated by internal drives that predispose them towards valuing certain results over others. Whereas normal humans usually value things like love, prosperity, and generation (some to greater degrees than others), Nephandi value hate, tragedy, and destruction.<br /> <br /> It's also for this reason that I don't dismiss the classic Nephandic trifecta of Infernalist/Malfean/K'llasshaa out of hand. Sure, I agree with Brucato in that many Nephandi would see no reason to follow Dark Powers. But I see that more as being for the same reason that normal people are sometimes atheists. They don't need some &quot;Absolute&quot; to justify their hate. They may even see such a thing as patently absurd, when the world is &quot;so obviously meaningless&quot;.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I can totally see other Nephandi taking a measure of comfort from worshiping a Dark Power. The gods that &quot;normal&quot; people serve reinforce many of the qualities that humanity as a whole desires; there are gods of love (and lust), justice, fertility, knowledge, and sport. For a Nephandus, these deities tend to look down upon at least some of the Nephandi's practices and desires. They can't relate to these religions, or to their adherents.<br /> <br /> The existence of Dark Gods, though, is a breath of foul air for a type of mage that has only known suffocating freshness and purity, to their dismay. A dark god encourages and validates a Fallen mage's feelings, and makes their urges seem almost right. For the Malfean mage, the Wyrm is the ultimate personification of blessed Death, calling upon those in the material world to slide everything towards oblivion. The K'llasshaa have their Great Ones, whose mentalities are as alien to the material world as the Nephandi feel themselves to be, or at least the Nephandi think so. Infernalists probably buy into the hype least, but they can probably empathize with beings for whom Evil is their only Good.<br /> <br /> Regardless of how sincere an individual Nephandus may be in service to the Dark Powers, there's something comforting about not being alone in their desire to further the cause of Greater Evil. This is also likely why, even if Nephandi can't stand each other, they aren't also at each other's throats (mostly). They may feel loathing for their peers (just as their loath humanity, life, and themselves), but those other Fallen bastards are also the only ones who really &quot;get it&quot;.<br /> <br /> So every bit of casual betrayal between Fallen &quot;buddies&quot; is taken in stride. They'll all come back in their next life to do it all again, so there's no point in letting hard feelings disrupt cooperation too much. And Nephandi have to become very used to doing unpleasant things (acting good, or tolerating other Nephandi) in order to fulfill their dark desires in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T08:11:09-07:00","id":1203837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203696#post1203696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nephandi believe that this particular version of reality is wrong, broken, corrupted and worthless. They want to see it destroyed so that a new reality can take its place. And they genuinely believe that this new version of reality will be an improvement over the previous one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nephandi never wanted to create a better world, from the first edition it was stated that they serve either Hell (as in, demons), the Wyrm, or alien lovecraftian horrors. Of these three, only the latter falls outside what we would call evil - unfortunately they're so alien that they would fall from what we call good too (and it's generaly accepted that making the world a better place for lovecraftian entities wouldn't be comfortable for us).<br /> <br /> Some extremist Euthanatos want to destroy the world and create a new, better, one. Sometimes Nephandi use this idea to corrupt Euthanatos (who's better to burn the world that satan, after all).<br /> <br /> If you think any of that (the pre M20 vision) is &quot;optimistic&quot; then you surely believe Black Spiral Dancers are misunderstood and the Garou nation it's the true antagonist faction in Werewolf :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T08:43:36-07:00","id":1203851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203837#post1203837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nephandi never wanted to create a better world, from the first edition it was stated that they serve either Hell (as in, demons), the Wyrm, or alien lovecraftian horrors. Of these three, only the latter falls outside what we would call evil - unfortunately they're so alien that they would fall from what we call good too (and it's generaly accepted that making the world a better place for lovecraftian entities wouldn't be comfortable for us).<br /> <br /> Some extremist Euthanatos want to destroy the world and create a new, better, one. Sometimes Nephandi use this idea to corrupt Euthanatos (who's better to burn the world that satan, after all).<br /> <br /> If you think any of that (the pre M20 vision) is &quot;optimistic&quot; then you surely believe Black Spiral Dancers are misunderstood and the Garou nation it's the true antagonist faction in Werewolf :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Depends on which kind of demon they're following, though. It sounds like we're assuming they serve an Earthbound, or a Ravener. But there are several factions among the Fallen who would be in favor of creating a better universe, and they collect worshipers just as much as the more sinister demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the BSD, I'm given to understand that prior to their corruption, they learned that the Wyrm was not an objective force of evil like they had been lead to believe, but rather it had become corrupted by yet another force of nature. And when they invoked its power, they did so to protect their lands from the invading Romans, who's plan was to enslave their people for their aggressively expanding empire.<br /> <br /> As for the Garou being the true antagonists... they did kind of fuck over Gaia with that whole War of Rage debacle.<br /> <br /> <br /> If the Nephandi were truly designed to be these objectively malicious beings who have no redeeming qualities at all, then why even give us the possibility of playing one?<br /> <br /> Nobody would want to play one, if all they do is go around spreading pain and suffering for its own sake.<br /> <br /> The fact that they can take comfort in the idea of a better universe, or support from a higher power is proof that they are not so far gone as to be mindless engines of destruction. Their trip through the Caul didn't destroy their essence or Avatar (or whatever), it merely altered them into a new state of being. A state that those of us who haven't gone through the Caul find completely alien to our way of comprehension. From an outsider's perspective, a Nephandi might seem like a slave to demonic forces. But from a Nephandi's perspective, they could be doing all of this completely of their own free will.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is something that they wanted to happen, that they <i>still want</i> to happen. Those smiles on their faces might not be ones caused by maniacal insanity, but genuine happiness stemming from the results of their work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember, the Nephandi absolutely despise this universe and everything it stands for. Of course they're going to do everything in their power to obliterate it. But if we replace it with something that they deem more agreeable, they might be willing to calm down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-06-2018, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T10:58:41-07:00","id":1203893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Nephandi were truly designed to be these objectively malicious beings who have no redeeming qualities at all, then why even give us the possibility of playing one? </div> </div> </div>In earlier editions, they didn't. And even in M20, their stance is \u201cwe can't stop you if you really want to; but we <i>strongly</i> advise against it.\u201d They don't so much \u201cgive the possibility of playing one\u201d as they recognize that it's impossible to forbid playing one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nobody would want to play one, if all they do is go around spreading pain and suffering for its own sake. </div> </div> </div> You'd think so, wouldn't you? Unfortunately, there are some people who <i>do</i> enjoy exactly that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-06-2018, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T11:57:01-07:00","id":1203927,"title":"","content":"Another nitpick: \u201cInfernalist\u201d and \u201cNephandi\u201d are closely related but distinct things. The defining feature of the Infernalists is that they serve demons (lowercase-d; not necessarily the Fallen or the Earthbound, but more generally \u201cevil spirits\u201d, \u201cOuter Gods\u201d, and similar things). The defining feature of the Nephandi is that they've had their Avatar inverted by a trip through a Caul, and are dedicated to tearing down Reality. You can be both Infernalist and Nephandus, or you can be one and not the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T12:04:54-07:00","id":1203933,"title":"","content":"Yeah, many Infernalists are just greedy idiots or desperate. It's entirely possible for an Infernalist to be a genuinely well intentioned person. They want to save the orphanage, they think they can get the power to do so by sacrificing a few goats, and then the demon spirals them into worse and worse trouble like a mafia loan shark. An Infernalist can easily be the result of a Breaking Bad scenario. Nephandi are much, much worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T01:28:14-07:00","id":1204142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1201891#post1201891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see this as short-sightedness. I see this as a difference in priorities.<br /> <br /> Sure, they've made it so humans can't feasibly travel vast interstellar distances to other worlds. But, by that same token, they've also made it so ALIENS can't either. The Consensus has been stacked towards there being other worlds, but against the likelihood of those beings being able to show up. A state of affairs that dictates the rules of engagement that outsiders can play by.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Consensus is local. The consensus on an alien world could be in favor of ftl travel allowing them to get here easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T01:34:13-07:00","id":1204143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204142#post1204142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consensus is local. The consensus on an alien world could be in favor of ftl travel allowing them to get here easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Consensus may be local, but so is the Gauntlet. And it doesn't care what beings from outside conventional space believe. The natives of this world believe there are astronomically vast distances between themselves and other hypothetical species. As such, that belief strengthens the Gauntlet against beings attempting to use &quot;Space Travel&quot; as a way of crossing over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T11:39:25-07:00","id":1204240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203851#post1203851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, the Nephandi absolutely despise this universe and everything it stands for. Of course they're going to do everything in their power to obliterate it. But if we replace it with something that they deem more agreeable, they might be willing to calm down.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just another lie they tell people. Usually mages who are on the brink of becoming Nephandi themselves, if they are seriously contemplating &quot;destroy all existence&quot; as a valid viewpoint to embrace. The caveat to replace the current universe with something better makes them feel they're walking into the Cauls for non-selfish reasons, but once they step out they're past any such illusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T13:33:54-07:00","id":1204278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204240#post1204240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's just another lie they tell people. Usually mages who are on the brink of becoming Nephandi themselves, if they are seriously contemplating &quot;destroy all existence&quot; as a valid viewpoint to embrace. The caveat to replace the current universe with something better makes them feel they're walking into the Cauls for non-selfish reasons, but once they step out they're past any such illusions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So that's it, then? They're just an objectively bad guy faction who want to end existence?<br /> <br /> I still find that difficult to comprehend, since they're pledging themselves to other forces. If the Nephandi only want to watch the world burn, then that would suggest their masters want the same thing. Otherwise, why would they transform them in such a way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T14:14:56-07:00","id":1204287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1202458#post1202458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, while it might be possible *purely technically* to colonize distant systems in RL right now, it would also involve<br /> <br /> 1) An insane sum of money.<br /> 2) An insane amount of planning.<br /> 3) People willing to go on a voyage that they, and a whole pile of next generations of their offspring, won't see the end of.<br /> 4) Trusting *those* generations to actually do the job down the line, which requires them properly preparing each that follows, along with upkeep of the vessel and self-sufficiency. Those generations would need to be trained and raised for that one very purpose, not with the mindset of &quot;I will give my offspring a happy life full of choices!&quot;. Because that generation and each that follows will only exist to maintain the vessel and prepare the next generation.<br /> 5) Hoping that all those generations will actually be able to handle anything like normal gravity, among things, because we have absolutely nothing like a human actually born in those conditions right now; And the effects on the physiology could be immense, starting with bones and the heart not growing to handle proper gravity.<br /> 6) Hoping that any repairs in this timespan necessary will not actually make the rest of the journey impossible, because there is no simple turning back. We already have a problem of modern computer systems being currently affected way too much by interstellar radiation, which is why so many computers up there are quite old models.<br /> 7) Hoping that supplies last, even with the ton of recycling, re-use and potentially necessary growth of food involved.<br /> 8) The will to do something like this, knowing that *we* on Earth also would (maybe) get to know the result of this whole endaevor only a whole pile of generations later, if we don't simply forget about it.<br /> 9) The pretty sure knowledge that the humans that might manage to colonize over there have as much in common with us as any society that, for hundreds of years, was separate and isolated from us.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> EDIT-BONUS:<br /> Also, since it's such a long trip, we would have to make the choice what technology we would pass along, including exact descriptions of how it works and how to build it, along with the principles behind it. As well as anything cultural we want to give them. And all of it would definitely need paper form along with multiple digital copies.<br /> <br /> Because those that would maaaaaaaaaybe manage to arrive there, and then maaaaaaaybe colonize there won't be able to reproduce multiple key technologies that are standard for us. For a long time. Like..well. Computers. Those that they have on arrival would be priceless artifacts.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <br /> So. It might be, in theory, technologically possible right now. But the way we would have to do it, *right now*, gives us absolutely zero reason to do so and would be an incredible risk and investment, to make a big understatement. All with a very very very high chance of &quot;Well, never heard of 'em again&quot;.<br /> <br /> Let's try Mars first. That's already a trip with incredible hardships for generations to come after arrival, if we ever plan to colonize, and many chances for things to horribly go wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> These are answered in the link in my first post. First this is happening in the far future, age retardation if not virtual immortality would be much different by then compared to now. So it is indeed very conceivable that the original travellers would survive a 112 year trip.<br /> <br /> 1. Yeah of course it will cost money but that is all relative, everything costs money and this will be a future that is ideally post scarcity because that is the nature of how things work once you have fusion, and you have access to off earth mining, its not an issue.<br /> <br /> 2. A feasible amount of planning, particularly if the Technocracy plans behind the scenes to help. But its a very feasible amount of planning.<br /> <br /> 3. Not an issue because by the time this is feasible its believed they would live that long, and even if they died their children would indeed survive it. Its believed by the time you figure out cryogenics you actually essentially have cracked all the problems involving staving off old age or reversing a failed body.<br /> <br /> 4. Yes you are essentially trusting people not to have terrorists among their children. They would heavily vet people that joined, stable healthy individuals. But sure there could be problems. But this won't be a crappy ship, the idea being roughing it on this ship is essentially living in a spacious large house for each individual with few people having to work more then 30 hours regularly. The ship will be large because its built in space. <br /> <br /> 5. The ship would have simulated gravity with centrifugal force, it wouldn't be much of an issue if programmed right, whats more of an issue is the fact that many planets are something like 80-90% Earth's Gravity would make people diverge over generations.<br /> <br /> 6. Unless you make a crazy doomsday catastrophe they would plan it so nothing major would breakdown and it would be self sufficient. And upon reaching the destination they could rebuild anything they needed including upgrading or replicating the ship.<br /> <br /> 7. Supplies will last, that is the truth of Fusion energy, and the space of the vessel. Unless someone terrorists the who vessel.<br /> <br /> 8. That's silly. They would be in constant communication, why wouldn't they? The ship will be traveling at a fraction of light speed and data will be faster then the ship on constant streams. Communication won't be instantaneous but it would all be relative what is considered a long wait. And why would they forget unless they had a super disaster on Earth? That is silly.<br /> <br /> 9. By the time they colonize they will likely be their own nation with their own charter. But they would be a foothold of humanity in that region and would provide trade and a place to travel too, particularly with other plans to expand. And with very much extended lifespans their will be a noticeable change in culture shift when someone is alive and reproducing in the same time as their Great Grand Kids reproducing.<br /> <br /> I mean I did post a link for a reason. All this is discussed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T14:16:23-07:00","id":1204288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204278#post1204278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that's it, then? They're just an objectively bad guy faction who want to end existence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204278#post1204278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still find that difficult to comprehend, since they're pledging themselves to other forces. If the Nephandi only want to watch the world burn, then that would suggest their masters want the same thing. Otherwise, why would they transform them in such a way?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a matter of fact, the various beings that the Nephandi claim to serve do indeed want to see the world burn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T15:18:10-07:00","id":1204314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204288#post1204288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a matter of fact, the various beings that the Nephandi claim to serve do indeed want to see the world burn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well if that's true, then what were these ancient forces of evil doing <i>before</i> humanity showed up and started influencing everything in their favor? I mean a bunch of these are supposed to predate us by many thousands of years, and yet the universe was still around by the time mortals arrived on scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T15:20:39-07:00","id":1204317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204314#post1204314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well if that's true, then what were these ancient forces of evil doing <i>before</i> humanity showed up and started influencing everything in their favor? I mean a bunch of these are supposed to predate us by many thousands of years, and yet the universe was still around by the time mortals arrived on scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other Mortals. Like Dinosaurmen of course!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T15:31:38-07:00","id":1204322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204317#post1204317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other Mortals. Like Dinosaurmen of course!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And Sharkmen, don't forget the immortal Sharkmen!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T16:29:27-07:00","id":1204333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204314#post1204314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well if that's true, then what were these ancient forces of evil doing <i>before</i> humanity showed up and started influencing everything in their favor? I mean a bunch of these are supposed to predate us by many thousands of years, and yet the universe was still around by the time mortals arrived on scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>They failed.<br /> <br /> Because &quot;the Neverborn won and destroyed existence&quot; means no WoD to play games in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T18:32:11-07:00","id":1204374,"title":"","content":"Also don't forget the Celestial Chorus' myths about the Pure Ones: if there's <i>any</i> truth to them, it's entirely possible that there were forces opposing these evil deities before humanity came on the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T18:37:23-07:00","id":1204376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204374#post1204374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also don't forget the Celestial Chorus' myths about the Pure Ones: if there's <i>any</i> truth to them, it's entirely possible that there were forces opposing these evil deities before humanity came on the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That was going to be my next question. Who was fighting the ancient evils before we came along?<br /> <br /> Because if they had free reign of the place and still couldn't get the job done, then they don't sound like much of a threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T02:25:07-07:00","id":1204478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1203851#post1203851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if we replace it with something that they deem more agreeable, they might be willing to calm down.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you think it is possible for other Nightfolk to reach some kind of agreement and understanding with the Nephandi ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204278#post1204278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that's it, then? They're just an objectively bad guy faction who want to end existence?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I read in the M:tA books, it doesn't seem so to me, at all. They seem like a faction of a type of Mages that would be called &quot;Black Mages&quot; by many ; if you need a criterion, then a definite one would be a large measure of contempt for mundane humans and disagreement with the idea of the so called &quot;Ascension&quot; . Additional qualities of the Nephandi seem to be a certain kind of selfishness, loyalty to one's group, and willingness to take risks.<br /> <br /> I think what makes the fact that the Nephandi don't want to ruin the world especially visible is that the three main factions of the Nephandi - the Infernal Nephandi, the Malfean Nephandi and the K'llasshaa Nephandi - seem to be capable of cooperating on a large scale and in a variety of ways. I think that a purely hostile faction agenda and goals would not have united such different and varied groups of Mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204278#post1204278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still find that difficult to comprehend, since they're pledging themselves to other forces. If the Nephandi only want to watch the world burn, then that would suggest their masters want the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 Core Book outright says that the Nephandi are not servile and that they don't serve the Nephandi patrons in the sense of having strict, very limiting obligations.<br /> The Nephandi Mages can relate to the Nephandi patrons in various ways - some could be called their majordomos or representatives ; others view the patrons as a distant source of inspiration, others see a way to learn more, for example through direct delving or contact, or by the way of comparisons and contrasting from afar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also you might ask from where comes the &quot;destroy the world&quot; part that often gets repeated in descriptions of Nephandi ? I would say it is either the Traditions' and the Technocracy's (and maybe other groups of Mages are also involved) propaganda, or maybe what the Nephandi tell to other Mages to scare them.<br /> Or maybe the Nephandi sometimes tell this and other things - or try to create such an impression, and other impressions - to other Mages to create a certain kind of atmosphere that definitely separates the Nephandi from other Mages, events and relations wise. The result is that the Nephandi Mages as a faction are in a kind of isolation, which benefits them in a variety of ways. For example it enables them to make recruitment into a multi-layered &quot;dark&quot; 'temptation' , that can also be done safely for both the recruiting Nephandus and the potential candidate. It is so much easier to arrange for safety of a potential Nephandus when all the friends of a Mage leave them and take five steps back while saying &quot;You joined the Nephandi, and they literally want to destroy the world !&quot; ; this reaction of shock makes arranging of safety easier.<br /> Imagine a Tradition Cabal trying to describe the Nephandi, with this extreme perspective of theirs, to a young, new Tradition Mage - this perspective of the Nephandi is so far away from truth and so blown out of proportion that the Tradition Mages are to an extent limited in their capabilities of acting against - both directly and indirectly - the Nephandi Mages ; due to, for example, their irrational outlook on the Nephandi faction and the Nephandi Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-08-2018, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T04:55:34-07:00","id":1204505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204478#post1204478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you think it is possible for other Nightfolk to reach some kind of agreement and understanding with the Nephandi ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> From what I read in the M:tA books, it doesn't seem so to me, at all. They seem like a faction of a type of Mages that would be called &quot;Black Mages&quot; by many ; if you need a criterion, then a definite one would be a large measure of contempt for mundane humans and disagreement with the idea of the so called &quot;Ascension&quot; . Additional qualities of the Nephandi seem to be a certain kind of selfishness, loyalty to one's group, and willingness to take risks.<br /> <br /> I think what makes the fact that the Nephandi don't wan't ruin the world especially visible is that the three main factions of the Nephandi - the Infernal Nephandi, the Malfean Nephandi and the K'llasshaa Nephandi - seem to be capable of cooperating on a large scale and in a variety of ways. I think that a purely hostile faction agenda and goals would not have united such different and varied groups of Mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> M20 Core Book outright says that the Nephandi are not servile and that they don't serve the Nephandi patrons in the sense of having strict, very limiting obligations.<br /> The Nephandi Mages can relate to the Nephandi patrons in various ways - some could be called their majordomos or representatives ; others view the patrons as a distant source of inspiration, others see a way to learn more, for example through direct delving or contact, or by the way of comparisons and contrasting from afar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also you might ask from where comes the &quot;destroy the world&quot; part that often gets repeated in descriptions of Nephandi ? I would say it is either the Traditions' and the Technocracy's (and maybe other groups of Mages are also involved) propaganda, or maybe what the Nephandi tell to other Mages to scare them.<br /> Or maybe the Nephandi sometimes tell this and other things - or try to create such an impression, and other impressions - to other Mages to create a certain kind of atmosphere that definitely separates the Nephandi from other Mages, events and relations wise. The result is that the Nephandi Mages as a faction are in a kind of isolation, which benefits them in a variety of ways. For example it enables them to make recruitment into a multi-layered &quot;dark&quot; 'temptation' , that can also be done safely for both the recruiting Nephandus and the potential candidate. It is so much easier to arrange for safety of a potential Nephandus when all the friends of a Mage leave them and take five steps back while saying &quot;You joined the Nephandi, and they literally want to destroy the world !&quot; ; this reaction of shock makes arranging of safety easier.<br /> Imagine a Tradition Cabal trying to describe the Nephandi, with this extreme perspective of theirs, to a young, new Tradition Mage - this perspective of the Nephandi is so far away from truth and so blown out of proportion that the Tradition Mages are to an extent limited in their capabilities of acting against - both directly and indirectly - the Nephandi Mages ; due to, for example, their irrational outlook on the Nephandi faction and the Nephandi Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm under no delusions that everything would be peaceful between everybody, nor even that most would agree with them. But I do believe that certain individuals or even groups of individuals would be in favor a new world envisioned by the Nephandi. Many of the antagonists factions such as the Sabbat, and the Thallain hate the current state of the world and wish for a return to how things used to be. When they were free to lord themselves over the world, instead of hiding in the shadows like lesser beings.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat only care about the Masquerade in the sense that it ensures their immediate continued survival. Their ultimate goal is to restore the world to a state prior to the inquisition, when vampires were free to act openly in society, and hideous Szlachta prowled the streets at night looking for spare parts.<br /> <br /> The Fomorians and their creations likewise ruled during a time of chaos and barbarism, before those pesky Tuatha taught mortals how to act like civilized beings. Reducing mortals back into primitive neanderthals wouldn't be so much 'destroying' the world for them, as it would be restoring it to its proper form.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, if we want to go even further, we could say that the new universe the Nephandi envision doesn't even have humanity in it. Mortals had their chance to rule the world and they royally fucked it up. As mages, the Nephandi could create a new universe where the monsters and other supernatural entities have alternative means of survival besides everybody relying on the same species.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">We're talking about entities who have the power to shape reality according to their will. </span></span></span>The possibilities are only limited by the player's imagination. Just because the universe that exists right now is going bye-bye doesn't mean there is no more World of Darkness. It just means we're getting a... New World of Darkness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah, I agree that the interpretation of the Nephandi is probably just overblown propaganda. There are two sides to every story and most people don't like to paint their enemies in a positive light. Traditionalists see the Technocracy as stifling and tyrannical. The Technocracy see Traditionalists as dangerous fools. If you're looking at things from their side of the fence, then sure, they might appear to be that way at first glance. But if you try to see things from the other side and explore their ideas further, it becomes clear that things are not so black and white.<br /> <br /> The reason they paint the Nephandi as such reprehensible beings is because nobody on their side is willing consider the idea that maybe the universe has run its course and that <i>we should</i> start over from scratch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hell, I just realized as I was typing this line that many of the ancient cultures believed in a cycle of destruction and recreation. The gods would create a universe, it would progress for a time, then once things were looking pretty messed up, they'd send down some event (like say, the End Times) to destroy everything. After which, the surviving powers would sweep up the pieces and build a new universe in its place.<br /> <br /> How do we know this cycle isn't sustained by the efforts of the Nephandi and their 'evil' patrons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-08-2018, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T05:16:02-07:00","id":1204509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204287#post1204287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are answered in the link in my first post. First this is happening in the far future, age retardation if not virtual immortality would be much different by then compared to now. So it is indeed very conceivable that the original travellers would survive a 112 year trip.</div> </div> </div> </div>I replied to your statement in the sense of it being possible to technologically reach those distant places as of right now, but not being feasable. It wasn't about the far future.<br /> In the far, far future things will surely be different. Also, as an aside, the '112 year trip' pretty much assumes the closest systems we can reach, which is probably not the most feasable set of places for any colonization due to the nature of the bodies found there. The trips would, very probably, take much longer.<br /> <br /> As I stated in a different post, I think our technology isn't even predictable a hundred years down the line, given our technological advances in just the *last* hundred years.<br /> But I do not doubt that sooner or later, we will attempt to colonize other systems, and that our technology will advance greatly.<br /> <br /> Still, I consider the video(s) behind the link also falling into Kurzweil's trap of ignoring the human element to a big degree, as well as pretty much painting an ideal development as something that will actually happen, despite nothing being set in stone yet regarding current theories and scientific attempts.<br /> But, let me go through a few points you just made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Yeah of course it will cost money but that is all relative, everything costs money and this will be a future that is ideally post scarcity because that is the nature of how things work once you have fusion, and you have access to off earth mining, its not an issue. </div> </div> </div>Fusion energy pushing us post scarcity does not quite connect. While we have a bit of an energy crisis right now, we seemingly have enough for people to build bitcoin farms that eat more energy than the population of Iceland, for fun and profit. The third world countries we have right now that are in bad shape are not in it because of a lack of energy, but many political and social factors, especially power-plays and economic abuse.<br /> Again: The human element, the thing that certain futurists are so good at ignoring and making it all about the tech.<br /> <br /> What fusion would definitely help with is engines of large space vessels however, and that is a big, big plus once we achieve it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Not an issue because by the time this is feasible its believed they would live that long, and even if they died their children would indeed survive it. Its believed by the time you figure out cryogenics you actually essentially have cracked all the problems involving staving off old age or reversing a failed body. </div> </div> </div>This borders very highly on speculation in several regards; That we actually figure out how to cryogenically freeze current human bodies without damage, and that we even decide to make people live that long. Overpopulation is already a problem. I am more consideringh what was said in another post earlier: If we ever colonize other places, we will probably take the steps to genetically engineer humans for the purpose. Being that will be, as the saying goes, more and less than what humans are right now, in order to offset the things technology cannot provide at that point, and that will also carry over to their offspring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Yes you are essentially trusting people not to have terrorists among their children. They would heavily vet people that joined, stable healthy individuals. But sure there could be problems. </div> </div> </div>I will get back to this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. Unless you make a crazy doomsday catastrophe they would plan it so nothing major would breakdown and it would be self sufficient. And upon reaching the destination they could rebuild anything they needed including upgrading or replicating the ship. </div> </div> </div>Nobody ever expects reliable technology to fail. Then it does, and you get catastrophes. Especially when it comes to technology that is supposed to last a trip of hundreds of years.<br /> <br /> As for them being able to rebuild everything on arrival, I think you are severely underestimating what that would require without a constant supply from earth.<br /> Having all the resources to build all the technology required to create a level of civilization and technology that we have on earth by then would literally require whole dismantleed factories being on that ship, along with the sheer knowledge to reassemble everything, AND operate and maintain it, among the crew.<br /> Not only that, but the resources required to build things would have to come not only on arrival from the ship's resources, but later on will require those resources to be native to the planet and to be available on the colony site - which, as I mentioned above, will probably not make the closest systems a viable option for colonization - and it will always be a gamble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. Supplies will last, that is the truth of Fusion energy, and the space of the vessel. Unless someone terrorists the who vessel. </div> </div> </div>This is the second time you use the term 'terrorist' for somebody whose decisions will sabotage the mission. I disagree that it would take terrorists. It would simply require the wrong decisions at the wrong time, coming from a society developing and changing away from us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 8. That's silly. They would be in constant communication, why wouldn't they? The ship will be traveling at a fraction of light speed and data will be faster then the ship on constant streams. Communication won't be instantaneous but it would all be relative what is considered a long wait. </div> </div> </div>Because at some point, the intervals between messages (and the reply back) will be measured in years, not days.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 9. By the time they colonize they will likely be their own nation with their own charter. But they would be a foothold of humanity in that region and would provide trade and a place to travel too </div> </div> </div>A foothold that is hundreds of years away. Which would also mean that any trade would take that long, as would any future travels.<br /> I agree that it would be a foothold of humanity, but I expect them to live very separate from us for a long time after that.<br /> By the time we, then, actually can travel to them quickly, it would very much be like visiting aliens that we will have to negotiate with again, with the added bonus of us sharing a homeworld when it comes to a peaceful outcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean I did post a link for a reason. All this is discussed. </div> </div> </div>It does not mean that I need to agree with the assumptions.<br /> Again, I *do* believe that in the far future we will attempt to colonize other systems. But I highly disagree that everything required will be ideally developed as it is assumed right now by some people, and I highly disagree that human nature and instinct won't cause a lot of trouble along the way. The picture painted is too clean and ideal.<br /> <br /> <br /> ....annnd that was mega-offtopic &gt;_&gt; Cough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-08-2018, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T05:27:25-07:00","id":1204511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204509#post1204509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, I consider the video(s) behind the link also falling into Kurzweil's trap of ignoring the human element to a big degree, as well as pretty much painting an ideal development as something that will actually happen, despite nothing being set in stone yet regarding current theories and scientific attempts.<br /> But, let me go through a few points you just made.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I also want to point out that not once in the entirely of human history has introducing a new species to a foreign environment worked out favorably for us. Every single time we've done it, it has had major consequences on the local ecosystem.<br /> <br /> Now we're considering transporting ourselves and presumably some other species from our planet to a new world that has never experienced our presence before. And we honestly expect that things are just going to turn out well for us if we do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-08-2018, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T08:28:53-07:00","id":1204560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204505#post1204505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, I just realized as I was typing this line that many of the ancient cultures believed in a cycle of destruction and recreation. The gods would create a universe, it would progress for a time, then once things were looking pretty messed up, they'd send down some event (like say, the End Times) to destroy everything. After which, the surviving powers would sweep up the pieces and build a new universe in its place.<br /> <br /> How do we know this cycle isn't sustained by the efforts of the Nephandi and their 'evil' patrons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there are groups in WoD with those kinds of beliefs, namely the Eastern Asia groups like the Kuei-jin and Beast Courts. However those beliefs are not shared across all of those groups and even those that do believe in it have different responses to it. Some do wish to speed it up, hoping to get to that second Golden Age faster. But others seek stop what they think is the impending Sixth Age, the darkest Age of the Cycle because... well it would mean a literal Hell on Earth for centuries or even millennia. And even then they'd have to go through several Ages of declining darkness before reaching it. Which is something most people don't want. How would you like if you were forced to live your entire like in a nightmarish version of Earth with only a vague promise that things will get better in a few hundred or thousand years?<br /> <br /> More than that, they don't believe that the world will end and something new and better will be created from the ashes, just that the world will eventually cycle back to better Ages.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that this is largely all belief and not something that we can one hundred percent pin down as true. The World of Darkness is built on Maybes and Could-Bes. To believe that the Nephandi are right, that world is a shitty, corrupt place and that only way to fix it is to burn it all down because the world will then remake itself from the ashes somehow is merely a step on the path to becoming a Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Hell, in <i>Ascension</i>, the MtAs Time of Judgement book, it's Nephandi Wins scenario has an Epilogue set a hundred or so years later sees Earth as a Hellscape ruled over by the Nephandi and their Patrons, torturing the Masses by their whims. The world as we knew it ended but it did not cease.<br /> <br /> Because I believe the entire idea of the universe being destroyed so that a better universe could emerge is a lie they tell. A false justification for their actions and a lie to tempt others to join them. Because their inverted Avatars do not seek Ascension but the Descent. To drag themselves and everyone around them downward into Hell as they conceive of it. Indeed, another <i>Ascension</i> scenario at the end that sees everyone Ascend and get what they want, sees the Nephandi all willingly dragged into their own Hells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T08:50:21-07:00","id":1204564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204560#post1204560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hell, in <i>Ascension</i>, the MtAs Time of Judgement book, it's Nephandi Wins scenario has an Epilogue set a hundred or so years later sees Earth as a Hellscape ruled over by the Nephandi and their Patrons, torturing the Masses by their whims. The world as we knew it ended but it did not cease.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you're making the mistake of judging their new world from the perspective of somebody raised in this one. You're not seeing things from the perspective of a Nephandi. Nobody said the Nephandi want to make the world better for everybody, just that they want to make the world better.<br /> <br /> And in this scenario, their version of 'better' is a universe free from moral obligation and societal expectations. A universe where they are free to indulge in every dark desire or perverse fantasy their corrupted hearts can dream up. Their victims may describe this scenario as a hellscape, but the Nephandi would call it a paradise.<br /> <br /> <br /> Come to think of it, this kind of discussion gives me some more insight into why playing a Path of Enlightenment is supposed to be difficult out of character. It's not enough to simply act in accordance with a path's tenets, you have to find a way to rationalize <b>why</b> your character believes in following that path.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-08-2018, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T08:52:31-07:00","id":1204565,"title":"","content":"The Euthanatoi and Verbenae also have beliefs involving cyclic time. From their perspective, the Nephandi aren't trying to hurry things along; they're trying to <i>break the cycle</i>.<br /> <br /> As for it all being propaganda: the chapter in M20 that describes the Nephandi makes the point early on that the writer is doing his utmost to provide objective facts in this chapter: any propaganda that creeps in does so despite his best efforts to weed it out. <br /> <br /> Which doesn't mean that you can't declare it to be propaganda in your games \u2014 as mentioned before, the book acknowledges that it can't dictate what you do with the game. But it's clear that the intent is to avoid providing biased information: when the book says that the Nephandi are bad news, that's not Tradition/Technocracy propaganda; it's as close to objective truth as exists in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T10:44:21-07:00","id":1204620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204376#post1204376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was going to be my next question. Who was fighting the ancient evils before we came along?<br /> <br /> Because if they had free reign of the place and still couldn't get the job done, then they don't sound like much of a threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe humans coming along was what gave them their first real foothold into the world. Nephandi, Spectres, Black Spiral Dancers, Baali, Pentex, Akuma, infernalists... these all come from the same place, and hint, it's not the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> Without agents to act on their behalf, cosmic horrors like the Neverborn <i>are</i> pretty powerless, at least where the material world is concerned. And humans have been making them powerful ever since the first caveman took a club to another caveman's skull just for ha has. That's one of the arguments the Nephandi make for how terrible humanity is. Evil did not exist until the advent of intelligent life.<br /> <br /> I've always believed that the fate of the WoD lies in humanity, for good or ill. They have the potential to destroy the Tellurian through mass Descension, like the Nephandi want to. They also have the potential to uplift it through mass Ascension.<br /> <br /> That's why Nephandi are the bad guys, dude. That's literally what they believe: all humans are bad guys. Things cannot ever get better, because humanity is just too flawed, and Ascension is a lie. The world is going to hell and we might as well enjoy the ride there. Cruelty to fellow humans is justified because human existence is unjustifiable.<br /> <br /> You can have them be tragically misunderstood or simply not totally wrong about everything in your games/headcanon. But as has been said, that's not how the developers wrote them.<br /> <br /> It's also a less interesting interpretation to me, as making the Nephandi unequivocally evil doesn't make them less compelling as characters. They aren't D&amp;D orcs. Every Nephandus was once a normal person (even the widderslainte, whose Avatars were inverted by other mages) who gave up on everything and succumbed to the cosmic blue screen of death. It's a fate that can happen to any mage and chilling proof that they can not only fail to Ascend, but make the world a whole lot worse by ever trying to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 04-08-2018, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T07:02:17-07:00","id":1204850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204505#post1204505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm under no delusions that everything would be peaceful between everybody, nor even that most would agree with them. But I do believe that certain individuals or even groups of individuals would be in favor a new world envisioned by the Nephandi. Many of the antagonists factions such as the Sabbat, and the Thallain hate the current state of the world and wish for a return to how things used to be. When they were free to lord themselves over the world, instead of hiding in the shadows like lesser beings.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat only care about the Masquerade in the sense that it ensures their immediate continued survival. Their ultimate goal is to restore the world to a state prior to the inquisition, when vampires were free to act openly in society, and hideous Szlachta prowled the streets at night looking for spare parts.<br /> <br /> The Fomorians and their creations likewise ruled during a time of chaos and barbarism, before those pesky Tuatha taught mortals how to act like civilized beings. Reducing mortals back into primitive neanderthals wouldn't be so much 'destroying' the world for them, as it would be restoring it to its proper form.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And yet Nephandi seem to want none of that. If they want to &quot;return&quot; to a prior state it would be to the prior state that existed before Creation. And that's a big IF, because most of the material point that they only want the void, much like Specters. Their Masters are just tools to bring that end closer but in the end, acording to M20, Satan it's going to be betrayed too - If Satan knows or cares about this it's an incognita.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat doesn't want that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or, if we want to go even further, we could say that the new universe the Nephandi envision doesn't even have humanity in it. Mortals had their chance to rule the world and they royally fucked it up. As mages, the Nephandi could create a new universe where the monsters and other supernatural entities have alternative means of survival besides everybody relying on the same species. </div> </div> </div>It won't have humanity nor the monsters we know. Nephandi may not be there either, but that's all the better because they want to end themselves if we go by they &quot;euthanize the universe&quot; argument<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yeah, I agree that the interpretation of the Nephandi is probably just overblown propaganda. There are two sides to every story and most people don't like to paint their enemies in a positive light. Traditionalists see the Technocracy as stifling and tyrannical. The Technocracy see Traditionalists as dangerous fools. If you're looking at things from their side of the fence, then sure, they might appear to be that way at first glance. But if you try to see things from the other side and explore their ideas further, it becomes clear that things are not so black and white. </div> </div> </div>If there is another side to this story I invite you to find it in any of the published material.<br /> <br /> Because we know the two sides of the Technocracy and the Traditions because the authors told us there's two sides (and it's ironical, because, you, who want so badly the Nephandi to be good as to blindly believe the first guy that tells you that while discarding the opinion of a lot of other people, were refusing to accept Technocracy as anything but the default bad guys a moment ago). The authors have told us over and over, OOC, that Nephandi are evil, a purely antagonistical, irredemable, faction - if you ever find something that unequivocally points to the other way, by all means point it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason they paint the Nephandi as such reprehensible beings is because nobody on their side is willing consider the idea that maybe the universe has run its course and that <i>we should</i> start over from scratch. </div> </div> </div>Where it's stated that the Nephandi want to &quot;start over from scratch&quot;? Not in M20. Perhaps if you preffer the old interpretation where they were the servants of hell - albeit even there it was implied that the Void was their ultimate goal (it was their Tenth Sphere and it was implied that their masters wanted the world to reach the state it was before creation). At the very least they want something that even the Sabbat (and half of the Baali) would find horrific, freeing the Wyrm/Satan/Cthulhu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, I just realized as I was typing this line that many of the ancient cultures believed in a cycle of destruction and recreation. The gods would create a universe, it would progress for a time, then once things were looking pretty messed up, they'd send down some event (like say, the End Times) to destroy everything. After which, the surviving powers would sweep up the pieces and build a new universe in its place. </div> </div> </div>Gues what? None of them have to be Nephandi. There's a lot of Traditionalists that believe in just that. Verbena and Euthanatos have whole factions of them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do we know this cycle isn't sustained by the efforts of the Nephandi and their 'evil' patrons? </div> </div> </div>While that may be a thing, Nephandi don't know that, if they're a tool of the cycle they're so unwillingly. If that's not the case find me a line where it's said that Nephandi are tring to restore or defend the cycle. Because M20 (and pretty much every published material since First Edition) says the oposite, OOC<br /> <br /> To put it bluntly, I'm more willing to believe that lizard people control the real world economy than to believe Nephandi were intended as anything but bad guys by the authors.<br /> <br /> I've already tackled the whole &quot;conspiration propaganda to make Nephandi the bad guys&quot; before, but to sumarize, if it was propaganda then even the authors themselves are being duped by the Traditions/Technocracy<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Depends on which kind of demon they're following, though. It sounds like we're assuming they serve an Earthbound, or a Ravener. But there are several factions among the Fallen who would be in favor of creating a better universe, and they collect worshipers just as much as the more sinister demons. </div> </div> </div>Oh. They don't follow Demon demons. Not even Raveners, albeit I think they should. As per Ascencion, Nephandi preffer other Demons.<br /> <br /> And not all Earthbound want the world to end. As far as I know, most of them just want the world to return to the prehistory where they were adored by millons, make evey human part of their cult, and kill all other demons that arent their thralls to be the focal point of that faith, and ultimately turn the world in their vision of paradise. (pretty much hell). Nephandi and Raveners, by contrast, seek the end of all (which might be moraly better than hell on earth depending on your point of view)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember, the Nephandi absolutely despise this universe and everything it stands for. Of course they're going to do everything in their power to obliterate it. But if we replace it with something that they deem more agreeable, they might be willing to calm down. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps - IF they want to murder the universe because it suffers, which it's a posibility - However, Nephandi strategy would seem to be &quot;You can't be in pain if there's not &quot;to be&quot; - pointing their fingers to the head&quot; - which it's, indeed, the Neverborn aproach to that particular problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-09-2018, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T07:32:37-07:00","id":1204859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204850#post1204850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've already tackled the whole &quot;conspiration propaganda to make Nephandi the bad guys&quot; before, but to sumarize, if it was propaganda then even the authors themselves are being duped by the Traditions/Technocracy</div> </div> </div> </div>It's usually even the other way around, ICly. The Traditions and Technocracy aren't trying to paint the Nephandi as evil - they probably resort to labeling infernalists and moral-less Mages as Nephandi to make hunting them down less red-tapey.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T10:23:58-07:00","id":1204900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204850#post1204850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snip*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay, except it was pointed out in one of the previous posts that the End Times scenario includes a prologue for what happens after the Nephandi win. It's <b>100 years later</b> and yet the universe hasn't been snuffed out of existence. So if you're looking for an example in the written material that the Nephandi don't explicitly want to reduce everything to the void, that right there is your example. The universe continues to exist, but now it's dominated by monsters, hence why Sabbat and Thallain might be amenable to forming an alliance.<br /> <br /> And if we go by the assumption that some of their masters used to be worshiped as gods, then there's also proof that faith in the Old Gods is restored once again, by the fact they've made their grand return to the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not desperately wanting the Nephandi to be good, I'm saying that those who are portraying them as these absolute doom bringers who have no ambitions beyond reducing everything to nothingness are probably over exaggerating. I don't think there's any other antagonists in World of Darkness who are designed to be so one dimensionally focused as the Nephandi are portrayed to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-09-2018, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T10:41:33-07:00","id":1204910,"title":"","content":"It's also possible that in timelines where the Nephandi start to win, they also start to lose their fanaticism and become corrupted by the tribalism and lazyness that corrupts every mass human movement.<br /> <br /> Humans are inherently tribal. We want wealth and power for ourselves, our families, and our friends, and we want to not need to work very hard to achieve it. That fundamental truth about humanity on the macro scale corrupts every other philosophy humans have ever espoused. It turns capitalism into crony-capitalism and oligarchy, because the first winners of the capitalist competition start using their power to stifle competition so they don't have to work very hard, and to give all the opportunities to the family and friends. It turns communism into a bureaucratic oligarchy, because the first people who achieve any bureaucratic power favor their families and friends, until all of the bureaucratic power is concentrated in the hands of a few lazy bureaucrats who are loyal to each other but otherwise sociopathic. And so on with theocracies or any other system you care to name.<br /> <br /> So maybe right now that the Nephandi are a tiny minority of underdogs, they really are fanatics for universal annihilation. But in timelines where they start to win, they get lazier and start enjoying the company of their fellow Nephandi, and start to think, &quot;why destroy the world, when I can just enslave and torture in, and enjoy the company of my fellow sadists?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T12:16:29-07:00","id":1204938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204900#post1204900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, except it was pointed out in one of the previous posts that the End Times scenario includes a prologue for what happens after the Nephandi win. It's <b>100 years later</b> and yet the universe hasn't been snuffed out of existence. So if you're looking for an example in the written material that the Nephandi don't explicitly want to reduce everything to the void, that right there is your example.</div> </div> </div> </div>You will always find contradictions if you conflate stuff from M20, Revised, and First. That scenario you mention was a callback to the first edition (with a first edition character <i>as the main antagonist</i>). Hence, as I stated (and you refused to listen):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where it's stated that the Nephandi want to &quot;start over from scratch&quot;? Not in M20. Perhaps if you preffer the old interpretation where they were the servants of hell - albeit even there it was implied that the Void was their ultimate goal (it was their Tenth Sphere and it was implied that their masters wanted the world to reach the state it was before creation). <b>At the very least they want something that even the Sabbat (and half of the Baali) would find horrific, freeing the Wyrm/Satan/Cthulhu.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>In this particular case, it was Cthulhu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The universe continues to exist, but now it's dominated by monsters, hence why Sabbat and Thallain might be amenable to forming an alliance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Al'Aswad released his Masters into the world and then got to rule with his Oracles as a reward. I don't know about the Thallain, but the Sabbat most certainly don't want a world controled by &quot;demons&quot; - they aren't allowing the Shaitan Baali nor Infernalists to enter their club, why would they tolerate Nephandi?.<br /> <br /> Unless you're telling me that Nephandi aren't slaves of their Masters as per M20 - but you don't want to do that because then this &quot;end world scenario&quot; doesn't hold water<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if we go by the assumption that some of their masters used to be worshiped as gods, then there's also proof that faith in the Old Gods is restored once again, by the fact they've made their grand return to the world. </div> </div> </div>Mage sometimes speaks about kingdoms of Nephandi and zigurats where the elder gods were worshiped, but it has a distintively lovecraftian take about it, much like the Baali birthplace, as it always speaks about unholy places of unholiness (some even say that Mages were created to fight against that) rather than actual old religions followed by sane people<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not desperately wanting the Nephandi to be good, I'm saying that those who are portraying them as these absolute doom bringers who have no ambitions beyond reducing everything to nothingness are probably over exaggerating. I don't think there's any other antagonists in World of Darkness who are designed to be so one dimensionally focused as the Nephandi are portrayed to be. </div> </div> </div>They're the BSD, Baali, Earthbound or Specters of the Mage setting.<br /> <br /> They're not <i>good </i>but they're as playable as anything with dots. All that I was saying it's that Nephandi are the &quot;doomsday&quot; faction, an antagonist faction made to kill at sight, not that they don't have more ambitions - the goal of their lot is to bring forth the apocalipse, and they're not ambiguous about that. They're evil and don't sugarcoat it with &quot;noble intentions&quot;, but that doesn't mean that they don't want stuff.<br /> <br /> Also, why is &quot;reducing everything to nothingness&quot; more one dimensional than &quot;Satan wins&quot;?. Every bad guy in WoD wants to release Satan, there's a &quot;demon&quot; behind every WoD plot. Nephandi just happen to have a more abstract goal than most.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also possible that in timelines where the Nephandi start to win, they also start to lose their fanaticism and become corrupted by the tribalism and lazyness that corrupts every mass human movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>You want to corrupt Nephandi with laziness. Really. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Nephandi: &quot;Stop yelling Master, I'm going to release you tomorrow&quot;.<br /> <br /> Master: &quot;But you ALWAYS say you're going to do it tomorrow&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-09-2018, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T12:44:21-07:00","id":1204944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204938#post1204938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Unless you're telling me that Nephandi aren't slaves of their Masters as per M20 - but you don't want to do that because then this &quot;end world scenario&quot; doesn't hold water<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe the other commenters explicitly said they weren't slaves. It's been brought up a few times that the Nephandi view their patrons as tools for getting what they want, and they are capable of operating with autonomy.<br /> <br /> As for the Baali, there's some debate over whether or not they're objectively evil. One side of the story says they perform sacrifices to empower and awaken their masters, while another story claims they do so in order to keep them placated and docile. That general of hell will be a lot less inclined to go on a ravenous eating spree if you feed him every day. It's a case of &quot;for the greater good&quot; at play there.<br /> <br /> <br /> And it was your very own post that stated not all Earthbound want to destroy the world, but rather remake it into their version of paradise.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Spectres, I don't see them as antagonists at all. They serve the void, and the void wants to reduce everything to nothingness? Okay, sure, but what are the alternatives? You spend an undetermined period of time trapped in the underworld with the constant threat of being turned into a coin, or a sword, or a doorknob, or a billion other inanimate objects because the Underworld doesn't have any natural resources. And then you're trapped in that state for eternity with no chance to cross over. I think ceasing to exist would be an act of mercy for those poor Wraiths.<br /> <br /> <br /> The reason I call them one dimensional is because you've basically been trying to tell me that the Nephandi are utterly, completely devoted on being evil for no other reason than the fact that they are evil. When all the other antagonist factions at the very least have some degree of sympathetic reason behind why they turned to evil.<br /> <br /> The Black Spiral Dancers may be hideously inbred servants of the Wyrm now, but the entire reason they turned to the Wyrm was to save their homeland from being enslaved to the Roman empire. Which they succeeded in doing, by the way.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Thallain want to spread chaos and savagery, because those are the dreams which sustain them. They were born in a time before civilization existed and when mortals started to dream of higher concepts beyond their immediate gratification, it confused the children of the Fomorians, prompting them to lash out against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-09-2018, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T13:14:53-07:00","id":1204957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204944#post1204944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I believe the other commenters explicitly said they weren't slaves. It's been brought up a few times that the Nephandi view their patrons as tools for getting what they want, and they are capable of operating with autonomy.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>What commenters explicitly steted was that, <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u>IN M20</u>, </span>was unequivocally stated that they weren't slaves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unless you're telling me that Nephandi aren't slaves of their Masters <span style=\"font-size:18px\">as per M20</span></b> - but you don't want to do that because<b><u> then this &quot;end world scenario&quot; doesn't hold water</u></b></div> </div> </div> </div>You're providing a (non canon, but official) example form <b>Revised </b>that contradicts <b>M20 </b>stance. M20 changes it's stance about Nephandi, as was mentioned countless of times in this thread. In that scenario it's explicitly mentioned that Aswad serves his <b>Masters</b>, and Nephandi are so enslaved by them that if they stop lending their power presto!, all Nephandi become unable to do magick. That may contradict M20, but it's no wonder since it's a story of Revised that's using a plot point from first edition<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You will always find contradictions if you conflate stuff from M20, Revised, and First. That scenario you mention was a callback to the first edition</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Baali, there's some debate over whether or not they're objectively evil. One side of the story says they perform sacrifices to empower and awaken their masters, while another story claims they do so in order to keep them placated and docile. That general of hell will be a lot less inclined to go on a ravenous eating spree if you feed him every day. It's a case of &quot;for the greater good&quot; at play there.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><u>Moloch </u>wants to keep them placated and docile and <u>Shaitan </u>perform sacrifices to empower and awaken them.<br /> <br /> <b>That's not two sides of A story, <i>that's two entirely different factions that want different things</i></b>, (or so they say). The faction that wants to perform sacrifices to empower and awaken their masters it's ALWAYS reffered as objectively evil.<br /> <br /> ALWAYS. If Moloch Baali were lying, and they were about awakening their masters too then they would be deemed as evil too, because it's that purpose what's evil.<br /> <br /> And that's what Nephandi want if they don't want to erase existence<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it was your very own post that stated not all Earthbound want to destroy the world, but rather remake it into their version of paradise. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and if you readed my post you should know that I said that Nephandi associate with similar beings. If they're slaves (most editions) or are using them to bring down the end of the universe (M20) it's ST choice<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Spectres, I don't see them as antagonists at all. They serve the void, and the void wants to reduce everything to nothingness? Okay, sure, but what are the alternatives? You spend an undetermined period of time trapped in the underworld with the constant threat of being turned into a coin, or a sword, or a doorknob, or a billion other inanimate objects because the Underworld doesn't have any natural resources. And then you're trapped in that state for eternity with no chance to cross over. I think ceasing to exist would be an act of mercy for those poor Wraiths. </div> </div> </div>And why you think it's an aberration to say that it would be a mercy for humans?. Why Nephandi wanting that causes you problems but Specters get a pass?<br /> <br /> Also, do you really think that Specters want Oblivion because they're at risk of becoming a coin?. Because Wraith implies that they want Oblivion because they're in constant suffering, much like their Neverborn masters, not because Stigian society it's evil.<br /> <br /> Why would be worse to seek oblivion if Wraith society was fairer? That wouldn't change Specters constant state of suffering. No, I think you want to paint specters as sympathetic &quot;rebels&quot;. That's why you want to make their evil a response to an external cause. That's not what Specters are in Wraith, you have the Renegades for that.<br /> <br /> What doesn't change in ALL editins of Mage it's that they're unequivocally evil and antagonistic - no sane moral system would condone their actions (a Blue &amp; Orange morality may, in some cases), those that serve Hell actually serve Evil because the demons they summon are Astral Spirits that are made of the very concept of evil.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-09-2018, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T14:03:26-07:00","id":1204972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204944#post1204944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Spectres, I don't see them as antagonists at all. They serve the void, and the void wants to reduce everything to nothingness? Okay, sure, but what are the alternatives?</div> </div> </div> </div>Transcendence.<br /> <br /> Pretty much all the arguments you've been making for why Nephandi/Spectres/Black Spiral Dancers/et al aren't bad guys are the same ones they make to string along dupes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Transcendence/Ascension/saving Gaia is too hard/a lie/not viable. Embrace Oblivion/Descension/the Wyrm.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T14:25:07-07:00","id":1204978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204972#post1204972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Transcendence.<br /> <br /> Pretty much all the arguments you've been making for why Nephandi/Spectres/Black Spiral Dancers/et al aren't bad guys are the same ones they make to string along dupes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Transcendence/Ascension/saving Gaia is too hard/a lie/not viable. Embrace Oblivion/Descension/the Wyrm.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What exactly is transcendence, though? Because the Wraiths don't actually know. They just know that the Underworld isn't the end of their journey and once they've cleaned up their business in this world, they get to move on to someplace else.<br /> <br /> As for Aleph asking about whether or not the Wraith society is corrupt, I would say very much so.<br /> <br /> What the hell do you need currency for? You're DEAD, your only focus should be resolving your unfinished business and moving on.<br /> <br /> Plus, according to the weird way that World of Darkness classifies the existence of a soul, there's a good chance that the Wraith isn't even the person who died in the first place, they're just an echo of them who's built an entire civilization from the tortured souls of those unlucky enough to have not transcended in time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember, in the Underworld, everything is made from a soul forged wraith. Every coin, every weapon, every article of clothing, every brick, every plank of wood, every tool and so on. Think about how many billions of souls that must have required over the thousand and thousands of years in order to build that place. And yet it's excusable because a mere handful of Wraiths get to transcend once in a while. Seriously, that place deserved to be wiped out by the Maelstrom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T16:51:52-07:00","id":1205012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204972#post1204972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much all the arguments you've been making for why Nephandi/Spectres/Black Spiral Dancers/et al aren't bad guys are the same ones they make to string along dupes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Transcendence/Ascension/saving Gaia is too hard/a lie/not viable. Embrace Oblivion/Descension/the Wyrm.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204978#post1204978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is transcendence, though? Because the Wraiths don't actually know. They just know that the Underworld isn't the end of their journey and once they've cleaned up their business in this world, they get to move on to someplace else.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's pretty much exactly how. &quot;Ascension/Transcendence is a big mystery. It could all be a fraud. Embrace the certainty of Descent/Oblivion, because at least you know what you're dealing with. And let's be honest, the current world/Underworld sucks too badly to even be fixable. Getting rid of it would be doing everyone a favor.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's your headcanon, and you don't have to abide by the writers' intention that those arguments are sophistry covering up what's essentially pure nihilism. Running a game where Descent/Oblivion isn't all bad would radically alter the tone of the setting, however, and turn the World of Darkness into the World of Solid Black. Even an all-Spectre chronicle in the normal WoD has some shades of light, as it at least presumes that Descent/Oblivion isn't a desirable state of existence.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want to play in a game where that isn't the case. It sounds too depressing. What's the <i>point </i>of anything the protagonists do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T17:01:34-07:00","id":1205014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1205012#post1205012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> covering up what's essentially pure nihilism.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not nihilism. Nihilism is the belief that moral meaning does not have the same objective reality as thermodynamics and 2+2 and so forth. Nihilism is essentially just a logical extrapolation on atheism. Nihilists are no more likely to want to destroy the world than anyone else. Nihilists are perfectly capable of being compassionate people, they just recognize that their compassion is a personal preference rather than something objective. Confusing nihilism with what the Nephandi espouse is the virtual equivalent of confusing atheism with satanism.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://imgs.xkcd.com/comics/nihilism.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-09-2018, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T17:47:40-07:00","id":1205024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1204978#post1204978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Aleph asking about whether or not the Wraith society is corrupt, I would say very much so.</div> </div> </div> </div>WHEN DID I ASKED THAT?<br /> <br /> I asked:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why Nephandi wanting (to end existence) causes you problems but Specters get a pass?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> do you really think that Specters want Oblivion because they're at risk of becoming a coin? </div> </div> </div>And finally:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would be worse to seek oblivion if Wraith society was fairer? </div> </div> </div>I never, ever, asked if Wraith society was corrupt. On the contrary, my question implies that Wraith society isn't very fair. I merely implied that <i>even if Wraith society WASN'T corrupt</i> Specters would still seek Oblivion because they want to die already and yet Death refuses to end their tormented souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-09-2018, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T17:52:35-07:00","id":1205026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1205012#post1205012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> And that's pretty much exactly how. &quot;Ascension/Transcendence is a big mystery. It could all be a fraud. Embrace the certainty of Descent/Oblivion, because at least you know what you're dealing with. And let's be honest, the current world/Underworld sucks too badly to even be fixable. Getting rid of it would be doing everyone a favor.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's your headcanon, and you don't have to abide by the writers' intention that those arguments are sophistry covering up what's essentially pure nihilism. Running a game where Descent/Oblivion isn't all bad would radically alter the tone of the setting, however, and turn the World of Darkness into the World of Solid Black. Even an all-Spectre chronicle in the normal WoD has some shades of light, as it at least presumes that Descent/Oblivion isn't a desirable state of existence.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want to play in a game where that isn't the case. It sounds too depressing. What's the <i>point </i>of anything the protagonists do?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In any case, even if we do go with the idea that Nephandi were created for no other reason than to have an enemy dangerous enough to make the Traditions and Technocracy call a cease fire, what was wrong with simply using the Marauders to fill that role? They're arguably just as dangerous, but can also be more complex and interesting than <i>&quot;Blaargh, I'm evil!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> My relationship with World of Darkness is conflicted. I love the general ideas it has, but I also find myself troubled by the concept that these supernatural and magical beings have declined to the point of being forced to hide from humanity just to survive. Dreaming is the game that resonates the strongest with me, and I find it to be the most depressing setting in the entire World of Darkness cosmology.<br /> <br /> I love the societies, characters, and abilities found in World of Darkness, but I also want to see them free to operate in public instead of hiding in the shadows. Which is a big reason why I like to play from the Antagonist point of view, since many of them are trying to make that kind of world come to fruition.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's the reason I'm starting to think about picking up Dark Ages, since the creatures there were allowed to operate with at least some level of freedom compared to the modern nights. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T17:55:06-07:00","id":1205028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1205024#post1205024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WHEN DID I ASKED THAT?<br /> <br /> I asked:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And finally:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I never, ever, asked if Wraith society was corrupt. On the contrary, my question implies that Wraith society isn't very fair. I merely implied that <i>even if Wraith society WASN'T corrupt</i> Specters would still seek Oblivion because they want to die already and yet Death refuses to end their tormented souls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry, I misinterpreted what you wrote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T20:35:27-07:00","id":1205075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1205026#post1205026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, even if we do go with the idea that Nephandi were created for no other reason than to have an enemy dangerous enough to make the Traditions and Technocracy call a cease fire, what was wrong with simply using the Marauders to fill that role? They're arguably just as dangerous, but can also be more complex and interesting than <i>&quot;Blaargh, I'm evil!&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Marauders don't have any real organization due to their nature. Yeah, you may get a band of Marauders running around causing mayhem but they don't have anything resembling anything close to real organization.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi on the other hand can and do. While they may not be as organized as the Traditions and Technocracy, there is a degree of organization and communication among the larger Nephandi groups. And there has been at least one instance of them gathering together in large numbers and wrecking havoc in a unified force, World War Two.<br /> <br /> Long story short, it got so bad that the Traditions and Technocracy had to officially unite to deal with the Nephandi threat. To date, that is the only time the groups have officially united, not the temporary team of a Cabal and Construct but a straight up partnership between the two organizations to deal with the threat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1205026#post1205026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My relationship with World of Darkness is conflicted. I love the general ideas it has, but I also find myself troubled by the concept that these supernatural and magical beings have declined to the point of being forced to hide from humanity just to survive. Dreaming is the game that resonates the strongest with me, and I find it to be the most depressing setting in the entire World of Darkness cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unsurprising. CtD is the most depressing game of the bunch. While it has the facade of being bright and cheerful, it is actually fairly depressing and bleak.<br /> <br /> That said, it's a mistake to consider the supernatural in decline and why they are hiding from humanity. Certainly the times have changed and the world's far cry from the halcyon days of legend but it's not all grim and bleak.<br /> <br /> To begin with, x20 has been showing the various splats better adapting to the modern world and moving away from this idea of a decline because how different the x20 Ed is from all the previous editions.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the Rev Ed was a countdown to the Time of Judgment and the end of the World of Darkness. As a result, the books of that line are all flavored by that. And all of that came from the fact that one of the things that went into the WoD when they were first designing it was the Millennium Scare of the 90's. But when you jump to the x20 Ed of the lines, much of that has been pushed aside, moved to the optional box because the world didn't end in 2004.<br /> <br /> In fact, the first MtAs book Onyx Path did were the four Rev Ed Convention Books that were never done before the WoD was originally ended. And in the Introduction Chapter of the first of those books, the NWO CB, they had this closing section talking about that and the setting of these new CBs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This book is first and foremost a love letter to the Mage: The Ascension fans who carried a torch for this wondrous world these many years. This book, for the most part, leaves off from the Iteration X book in 2001.<br /> <br /> In another reality, the Time of Judgment came, a Red Star its herald. The world ended, either through mass Ascension, war, or catastrophe. Yet, here we are in 2012, our world for the moment still spinning. For us, the Red Star was not a harbinger of doom, but a passing moment of curiosity, instilling dread in those most paranoid. Our destinies certainly changed, and we can only hope for the better.<br /> <br /> The world didn\u2019t get off scot-free, though. The Avatar Storm continues to savage the Horizon realms, cutting the Traditions and Technocrats alike off from their leadership. Some of those possible fates from that other reality hover over ours like the Sword of Damocles, particularly a Technocratic civil war. As for the rest of the details in the Time of Judgment, such as the Rogue Council and the Panopticon, maybe they\u2019re in your chronicle\u2019s future. According to one<br /> school of thought, \u201cJudgment Day is inevitable.\u201d But another says there is no fate but what we make.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll leave to you Storytellers the task of merging those timelines. This book is about our reality, today, and all that\u2019s transpired to bring us to this glorious moment. </div> </div> </div>And that really is the x20 Ed thoughts on the Time of Judgement and the end of the world that everything seemed to heading towards. In one world, it did happen but that world isn't the x20 world. The signs and portents of doom, if they happened at all, were but a passing curiosities rather than warnings of what was to come.<br /> <br /> Hell, W20's opening turned the Prophecy of the Phoenix, the big dreaded prophecy of the Apocalypse from a warning of doom into a call to arms. That this is not the time to give up and swallowed up by despair, that by standing firm and fighting they can, they <i>will</i> be victorious.<br /> <br /> As others have mentioned, you have to keep a degree of separation between Editions, especially with the x20 Ed and the previous Editions.<br /> <br /> Beyond that however, most of the Splats have reasons for keeping themselves hidden from humanity. Vampires have always been outnumbered by humans and especially in this modern age, with all the weapons we have, they fear the outcome of the Masquerade falling and humanity going to war with them because despite all their powers man can do a LOT of damage. Hell, the Inquisition back in it's day gave them quite a scare with the damaged they caused hundreds of years ago.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are held back by the Delirium and the laws of the Litany. Even if they disregard the Litany, they can't go walking around in public in any form other than wolf or human because if ordinary people see them, the vast majority will go into a state of shock or temporary insanity at the sight of them.<br /> <br /> Mages have the whole Paradox issue restricting them from fully utilizing their Magic safely, both for themselves and others.<br /> <br /> Wraiths largely exist in a separate world from the living, with limited means of engaging with the living.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1205026#post1205026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the societies, characters, and abilities found in World of Darkness, but I also want to see them free to operate in public instead of hiding in the shadows. Which is a big reason why I like to play from the Antagonist point of view, since many of them are trying to make that kind of world come to fruition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the World of Darkness is supposed to be just like our world but darker. We don't have vampires, werewolves, mages, changelings, wraiths etc. Having the supernatural out in the open will fundamentally alter the world as we know it. If the supernatural has always been out in the open, the modern WoD wouldn't be anything like our world. Hell, the various groups within the splats probably wouldn't exist either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1205026#post1205026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the reason I'm starting to think about picking up Dark Ages, since the creatures there were allowed to operate with at least some level of freedom compared to the modern nights. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not as much as you think. The divide between Man and the Supernatural is certainly thinner than in the modern times but it is still there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T12:44:45-07:00","id":1208981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1205075#post1205075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Nephandi on the other hand can and do. While they may not be as organized as the Traditions and Technocracy, there is a degree of organization and communication among the larger Nephandi groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nephandi as a faction of Mages do seem to me somehow more efficiently and deeply ( I am not sure if 'deeply' is the right adjective to use ) organised than the Traditions, and the Technocracy. They have four ranks, five if you count the Aswadim ; and each rank has a clear and distinct role and focus. The Nephandi manage to consistently and regularly find, recruit ( and sometimes Awaken to being Mages ) Widderslaintes. Their capabilities and membership has increased over the centuries, despite being less numerous than the Traditions, and the Order of Reason and later the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-19-2018, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T13:41:12-07:00","id":1209002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1205075#post1205075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Except the World of Darkness is supposed to be just like our world but darker. We don't have vampires, werewolves, mages, changelings, wraiths etc. Having the supernatural out in the open will fundamentally alter the world as we know it. If the supernatural has always been out in the open, the modern WoD wouldn't be anything like our world. Hell, the various groups within the splats probably wouldn't exist either.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, it's supposed to be our world, but it didn't start out that way. A lot of the different splats have lore regarding times when people knew about their existence, and they were (mostly) free to operate. It either took some sort of cataclysmic event, or many millennia worth of human development to force them into hiding. The antagonist groups want to fight against these changes and restore things to how they used to be.<br /> <br /> Even if it is realistically impossible, the narrative of a once powerful race / civilization trying to reclaim its former glory is a story I find to be more engaging than playing as a metaphor on the negative aspects of the human condition. Except for Changeling: the Dreaming, since the narrative manages to combine both of those stories into one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T06:53:43-07:00","id":1209224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1209002#post1209002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Right, it's supposed to be our world, but it didn't start out that way. A lot of the different splats have lore regarding times when people knew about their existence, and they were (mostly) free to operate. It either took some sort of cataclysmic event, or many millennia worth of human development to force them into hiding. The antagonist groups want to fight against these changes and restore things to how they used to be.<br /> <br /> Even if it is realistically impossible, the narrative of a once powerful race / civilization trying to reclaim its former glory is a story I find to be more engaging than playing as a metaphor on the negative aspects of the human condition. Except for Changeling: the Dreaming, since the narrative manages to combine both of those stories into one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's untrue.<br /> <br /> Or rather, it's true only for the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Traditions want humans to know about magick to create a new Mythic Age, they're making in baby steps towards that goal because they want to avoid a possible Inquisition and because the Technocracy doesn't want that and crushes their efforts with an iron fist, but the end goal of the Traditions it's and has always been to work in the open.<br /> And Traditions were always protagonist, even in the old days when the Technocracy was just an antagonist faction (that wanted and still wants the opposite you're stating), and they're still protagonists.<br /> On the other hand Nephandi are pretty OK with Modernity. They don't have anything against the mythic age and ruling in the open either, but they don't <i>need </i>to rule in the open to reach their goal. They almost won in WW2, they were defeated by a hair split and an improbable alliance. And if M20 it's right they may still be the ones winning the War, under the guise of the Tech-heads.<br /> And Marauders, only god knows what they want (but some seem to want the world to return to a more Wyld state - Note that fight against the Nephandy and the Technocrats more than they do against the Traditions and Disparate)<br /> <br /> Most factions of Demons want to rule the world in the open like they did in the time before the Fall. Only the Redeemers (because God forbide such interaction) and the Ravagers (because a strong Demon society could prevent them from unmaking Creation) don't want that - and these two are presented in a much more atagonistical fashion than the Luciferian, who totally want to be loved by an enlightened humanity<br /> <br /> In Wraith the Hierarchy wants things to be as they are, but the Renegades and Heretics do want to interact with the living, and they aren't strictly speaking &quot;antagonist factions&quot;.<br /> Specters are antagonists and they don't care abaut anything but to send everything to Oblivion, for that purpose nothing could be worse than to return to the old days were the Maelstrom wasn't a thing and people had a different relationship with death.<br /> <br /> Some members of the Garou Nation (like the Red Talons) want to go back to the Impergium (and some like the COG want a peaceful relationship with humans). Many Fera wish to have the pressence and power than they lost at the hands of the Garou. All of them have myths about an &quot;age of glory&quot; before everything went south.<br /> The antagonists factions want none of that. BSD and Pentex are pretty happy about the developments of last century because the Wyrm it's almost free. The forces of the Weaver want things to keep progressing as they are now too, but with less corruption. Their goals either aren't compatible with &quot;restoring things to how they used to be&quot; or can be achieved either way.<br /> <br /> In Changeling NO ONE want's to protect the status quo - the status quo it's literally killing you. They just have different ideas about what &quot;to fight against these changes&quot; trully means (and some Unseelie don't care, but even them tend to care).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-20-2018, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T07:39:32-07:00","id":1209240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1209224#post1209224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> In Changeling NO ONE want's to protect the status quo - the status quo it's literally killing you. They just have different ideas about what &quot;to fight against these changes&quot; trully means (and some Unseelie don't care, but even them tend to care).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While most of the others were good points, I have to disagree with this one, since Most of what I've read about the setting supports my previous assessment. Particularly the behavior of the Arcadian Sidhe and the Dreaming itself. According to the backstory, the Dreaming supports the structure of the Sidhe ruling over the commoners, regardless of what the rest of the world thinks. Once they showed up, they demanded a return to the old ways, and despite the commoners adamantly refusing, the Dreaming complied to their demands without a struggle. Nobles were born to rule, and the commoners were born to serve.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Fae aren't people in the conventional sense. The nobles don't aspire to greatness, they are greatness. They are what mortals think about when they hear the word 'greatness.' Nobody has dreams of becoming king, only to bow in fealty to the town blacksmith, or the court jester.<br /> <br /> <br /> Plus, the deeper you wander into the Dreaming, the more your fae nature begins to manifest. C20 outright states that nobles become increasingly less empathetic towards commoners, and by the time they manage to reach the Deep Dreaming, they can barely stand to be in the same room as each other. That doesn't sound like the mentality of somebody who wants equality for all, but rather it sounds like they are most displeased with the current state of affairs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, at least one of the end of the world scenarios has the fae abandoning the Autumn World completely and returning to Arcadia with the help of House Danaan. This event also may or may not involve their faerie souls being purified of Banality in the process, thus allowing them to cast off the influence of mortal society and return to their original states.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:51:19-07:00","id":1209274,"title":"","content":"But wasn't your argument: &quot;I like antagonists because they want to return to the old ways&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">. A lot of the different splats have lore regarding times when people knew about their existence, and they were (mostly) free to operate. It either took some sort of cataclysmic event, or many millennia worth of human development to force them into hiding.<b> The antagonist groups want to fight against these changes and restore things to how they used to be</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, the deeper you wander into the Dreaming, the more your fae nature begins to manifest. C20 outright states that nobles become increasingly less empathetic towards commoners, and by the time they manage to reach the Deep Dreaming, they can barely stand to be in the same room as each other. That doesn't sound like the mentality of somebody who wants equality for all, but rather <b>it sounds like they are most displeased with the current state of affairs</b>. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. They aren't an &quot;antagonist faction&quot;, they hate modernity with a passion, and they want to go back to the old ways. They've even achieved success in crushing the Commoners (that also wanted to change the world, but not always to return to the old ways). They're the epitome of &quot;a once powerful race / civilization trying to reclaim its former glory&quot;, and they've almost made it (if only Banality/Beldam wasn't such a party pooper).<br /> <br /> These protagonists aren't of your liking because they aren't <b><i>egalitarian </i></b>or just because many of them want to throw the towel and get back to Arcadia instead of changing the world?.<br /> <br /> As far as I know, the seeking of Arcadia it's deemed as something practically impossible. And also there's the problem that the Shide either fleed or were expulsed from Arcadia - which makes return a hazardous goal (as far as we know, Arcada has fallen or may not want the Shide back). Sure, some protagonists try to find it, but most try to survive in a world that's killing them and would like the world to return to a friendlier state","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-20-2018, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T09:36:14-07:00","id":1209288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1201880-is-the-technocracy-short-sighted?p=1209274#post1209274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But wasn't your argument: &quot;I like antagonists because they want to return to the old ways&quot;?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I mostly speaking about me playing games in general, not just about classic World of Darkness specifically. From what I can tell, Chronicles of Darkness seems to be more in theme with my previous argument as they have various groups who stand on the side of the 'monsters' rather than humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regardless, I don't own all the splat books, and the ones I do own, I only have the core books for them. So if any of the various factions have grander motives, I don't claim to have knowledge about them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}